hadiths[368]{hadithnumber,text}:
"8907","Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, said on the Day of Jamal that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, did not covenant to them any covenant to take regarding rule, but it was a matter of their own opinion. Then Abu Bakr, may Allah have mercy on him, was made successor and he established and remained upright, then Umar, may Allah have mercy on him, was made successor and he established and remained upright until religion became firmly settled."
"8908","Abd Khayr reports that Ali ibn Abi Talib stood on the minbar and mentioned the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. He said that the Messenger of Allah was taken, then Abu Bakr was made successor and acted by his action and followed his way until Allah took him in that state, then Umar was made successor and acted by the action of both and followed their way until Allah took him in that state."
"8909","Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that it was said, O Messenger of Allah, whom shall we appoint after you. > **""If you appoint Abu Bakr you will find him trustworthy, detached from this world and desirous of the Hereafter. If you appoint Umar you will find him strong and trustworthy, whom no blame of a blamer overtakes regarding Allah. If you appoint Ali, and I do not see you doing so, you will find him guiding and guided, taking you upon the straight path.""**"
"8910","Hudhayfah ibn al-Yaman, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that they said, O Messenger of Allah, will you not appoint a successor over us. > **""If I appoint a successor over you and you disobey my successor, punishment will descend upon you. If you appoint Abu Bakr you will find him weak in body but strong in the affair of Allah. If you appoint Umar you will find him strong in body and strong in the affair of Allah. If you appoint Ali, and you will not do so, he will take you upon the straight path, and you will find him guiding and guided.""**"
"8911","Aishah, may Allah be pleased with her, reports that when the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, founded the mosque of Madinah he brought a stone and placed it, then Abu Bakr brought a stone and placed it, then Umar brought a stone and placed it, then Uthman brought a stone and placed it. When asked about that he said. > **""This is the affair of the caliphate after me.""**"
"8912","Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, entered a garden and one came knocking. He said, O Anas, rise and open for him and give him glad tidings of Paradise and of the caliphate after me, and it was Abu Bakr. Then another came and he said, O Anas, open and give him glad tidings of Paradise and of the caliphate after Abu Bakr, and it was Umar. Then another came and he said, O Anas, open and give him glad tidings of Paradise and of the caliphate after Umar and that he will be killed, and it was Uthman. Uthman entered and said, O Messenger of Allah, why, by Allah I have never been insolent nor wished nor touched my private part since I pledged to you. > **""O Anas, rise and open for him and give him glad tidings of Paradise and of the caliphate after me. It is so, O Uthman.""**"
"8913","Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, reports that in the lifetime of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, they used to say Abu Bakr, Umar and Uthman, meaning regarding the caliphate."
"8914","Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, reports that in the lifetime of the Messenger of Allah they used to say, who is most worthy of this affair, and they would say Abu Bakr. Then they would say, if Abu Bakr is taken, who is most worthy, and they would say Umar ibn al-Khattab. Then they would say, if Umar is taken, who is most worthy, and they would say Uthman."
"8915","Abu Khidash ibn Umayyah, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that he sought a need from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said, if I do not find you. > **""Then come to Abu Bakr. Then come to Umar. Then to Uthman.""** He said, if I do not find Uthman, he fell silent, and he repeated it twice or thrice, and he said to himself, that is the bounty of Allah which He gives to whom He wills."
"8916","Jarir, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that when the Messenger of Allah came to Madinah he said to his Companions, come with us to the people of Quba to greet them. He said, O people of Quba, bring me stones from this lava ground, and many stones were gathered, and with his spear he marked their qiblah. He took a stone and placed it, then said. > **""O Abu Bakr, take a stone and place it by my stone. O Umar, take a stone and place it by the stone of Abu Bakr. O Uthman, take a stone and place it by the stone of Umar. Let each man place his stone where he loves upon that line.""**"
"8917","Safinah, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that a man said, O Messenger of Allah, I saw as if a scale was let down from heaven and you were weighed against Abu Bakr and you outweighed, then Abu Bakr against Umar and Abu Bakr outweighed, then Umar against Uthman and Umar outweighed, then the scale was lifted. The Messenger of Allah interpreted it as the caliphate of prophethood, then Allah gives kingship to whom He wills. > **""It is the caliphate of prophethood, then Allah shall give kingship to whom He wills.""**"
"8918","Abdullah ibn Amr, may Allah be pleased with them both, reports that he heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say. > **""There shall be after me twelve caliphs, among them Abu Bakr al-Siddiq who shall not remain after me but little, and the master of the millstone of the Arabs who shall live praiseworthily and die as a martyr. He is Umar ibn al-Khattab. O Uthman, if Allah clothes you with a shirt and the people want you to remove it, do not remove it, for by Allah if you remove it you shall not see Paradise until the camel passes through the eye of the needle.""**"
"8919","Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, reports concerning the saying of Allah, when the Prophet confided to one of his wives a statement, that Hafsah entered upon the Prophet in her house while he was with Mariyah. The Messenger of Allah said to her, do not inform Aishah until I give you glad tidings that your father will rule after Abu Bakr when I die. Hafsah told Aishah what she saw and what he told her that Abu Bakr will follow the Messenger of Allah and Umar after him. Aishah said to the Prophet, who informed you this, he said the All-Knowing, the All-Aware informed me. Aishah said, I shall not look at you until you forbid Mariyah, so he forbade her, and Allah revealed, O Prophet, why do you forbid what Allah has made lawful for you. > **""Do not inform Aishah until I give you glad tidings. Your father shall rule after Abu Bakr when I die. The All-Knowing, the All-Aware has informed me.""**"
"8920","Ismah, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that a man of Khuzaah came and Ali met him and asked what brought him. He said, I came to ask the Messenger of Allah to whom we should pay the charity of our wealth when Allah takes you. The Prophet said, to Abu Bakr. He said, if Abu Bakr is taken, to whom. He said, to Umar. He said, if Umar is taken, to whom. He said, to Uthman. He said, if Uthman is taken, to whom. > **""To Abu Bakr. To Umar. To Uthman. Look to yourselves.""**"
"8921","Ismah, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that a bedouin came with camels and the Messenger of Allah bought them on credit. Ali told him to return and ask, O Messenger of Allah, if something happens to you who will settle my due, and inform Ali of the answer. He said Abu Bakr. Ali sent him again, if something happens to Abu Bakr who settles, he said Umar. He sent him again, when Umar dies who settles, and the Messenger of Allah said. > **""Abu Bakr. Umar. Woe to you, when Umar dies, if you are able to die then die.""**"
"8922","Hudhayfah, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that the Messenger of Allah was taken, then Allah made Abu Bakr successor, then Abu Bakr was taken and Allah made Umar successor, then Umar was taken and Allah made Uthman successor."
"8923","Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, reports that when the Messenger of Allah died the Muslims looked to their best and made him successor, and he was Abu Bakr. When he died they looked to the best of the Muslims and made him successor, and he was Umar. When Umar died or was killed they looked to their best and made him successor, and he was Uthman. He said, if you kill him then bring me one better than him, by Allah I do not see you doing so."
"8924","Abu Dharr, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that they were with the Prophet and he took pebbles which glorified in his hand, then fell silent when laid down. He gave them to Abu Bakr and they glorified in his hand, then to Umar and they glorified, then to Uthman and they glorified, then to Ali and they fell silent when laid down. Al-Zuhri said, it is the caliphate which Allah gave to Abu Bakr, Umar and Uthman."
"8925","Al-Numan ibn Bashir, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that Zayd ibn Kharijah fell dead between noon and afternoon and was shrouded, and between Maghrib and Isha women gathered wailing when a voice from beneath the cover said twice, be silent O people. His face and chest were uncovered and he said, Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah, the unlettered Prophet, the seal of the prophets, it was in the Book. Then it was said upon his tongue, he spoke truth, Abu Bakr al-Siddiq is the caliph of the Messenger of Allah, strong and trustworthy, weak in body strong in the affair of Allah, it was in the first Book. Then he said, Abdullah Umar is Commander of the Believers who fears no blame, who prevents the strong from devouring the weak. Then he said, Uthman is Commander of the Believers, merciful to the believers. Two have passed and four remain, people differ with no order, sanctities are violated, the Hour draws near and people devour one another."
"8926","Al-Numan ibn Bashir, may Allah be pleased with him, reports in a variant that when Zayd ibn Kharijah died he waited for Uthman to come out thinking he prays two rakahs, the cloth was lifted from his face and he said, peace be upon you, peace be upon you, while the household spoke. He said glory to Allah in prayer, and he said, be silent, be silent, and the rest is similar."
"8927","Abu al-Tufayl, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said. > **""I saw in sleep as if I draw water from a land and black sheep and dusty sheep came to me. Abu Bakr came and drew one or two buckets with weakness in them, may Allah forgive him. Then Umar came and drew and it became a large bucket, filling the basin and watering the arrivals. I never saw a strong man drawing better than Umar. I interpreted the black as the Arabs and the dusty as the non-Arabs.""**"
"8928","Hudhayfah, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that the Messenger of Allah was sent to the Arabian Peninsula and filled it with equity and justice, then Abu Bakr carried them in a pleasing journey, then Umar carried them in a pleasing journey."
"8929","Said ibn Yahya from his father reports that Hafsah said, O Messenger of Allah, when you were ill you advanced Abu Bakr. > **""It is not I who advanced him, but Allah who advanced him.""**"
"8930","Abdur Rahman ibn Abi Bakr, may Allah be pleased with them both, reports that the Messenger of Allah said. > **""Bring me an inkpot and a shoulder blade that I may write for you a book after which you shall never go astray.""** Then he turned his back and faced them and said. > **""Allah and the believers refuse but Abu Bakr.""**"
"8931","Al-Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that he entered upon the Messenger of Allah while his wives were with him and they veiled except Maymunah. He said, none who witnessed the ladud in the house shall remain but be given it, except my oath did not reach al-Abbas. Then he said, order Abu Bakr to lead the people in prayer. Aishah said to Hafsah, tell him Abu Bakr is a man who weeps when he stands in that station. He repeated, order Abu Bakr to lead the people. Abu Bakr led, then the Prophet felt lightness and came, Abu Bakr stepped back, but he sat beside him and recited. > **""Order Abu Bakr to lead the people in prayer.""**"
"8932","Sahl ibn Sad, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that there was discord among the Ansar and the Messenger of Allah went to reconcile them, then returned after prayer was established with Abu Bakr leading, and the Messenger of Allah prayed behind Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him."
"8933","Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that when the Messenger of Allah fell ill with his fatal illness Bilal came to announce prayer. After twice he said, O Bilal, you have conveyed, so whoever wishes let him pray and whoever wishes let him leave. Bilal returned and said, may my father and mother be for you, who shall lead. He said, order Abu Bakr to lead the people. When Abu Bakr advanced the curtains were lifted and they saw him as a white leaf upon a garment. Abu Bakr stepped back thinking he would come out, but the Messenger signaled him to stand and pray, so Abu Bakr led, and they never saw him after. > **""O Bilal, you have conveyed, so whoever wishes let him pray. Order Abu Bakr to lead the people.""**"
"8934","Buraydah, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that the Messenger of Allah fell ill and said, order Abu Bakr to lead the people. Aishah said, O Messenger of Allah, my father is a tender man. He said, order Abu Bakr to lead the people, for you are like the companions of Yusuf. So Abu Bakr led while the Prophet was alive. > **""Order Abu Bakr to lead the people in prayer, for you are like the companions of Yusuf.""**"
"8935","Salim ibn Ubayd of the people of Suffah reports that the Messenger of Allah fainted in his illness then awoke and asked, has prayer come, they said yes. He said, order Bilal to call and Abu Bakr to lead. Aishah said, my father is tender-hearted, order another. He fainted again and repeated the same. Then he asked, has prayer been established, they said yes. He said, bring a man I may lean upon, so Buraydah and another came and he entered the mosque while Abu Bakr led. Abu Bakr stepped aside but the Messenger prevented him and sat beside him till he finished. When the Messenger died Umar said, I shall strike with the sword whoever says he died. Abu Bakr took his arm and said, you are dead and they are dead, and they asked, has he died, prayer over him, where to bury, and he said, where he was taken, for Allah took him only in a good spot. Then the Muhajirun gathered saying, go to our brothers of the Ansar, and an Ansari said, from us an amir and from you an amir. Umar took Abu Bakr's hand and asked, who has these three, the second of two in the cave, when he says to his companion grieve not, Allah is with us, who is his companion. He struck his hand and said, pledge him, and they pledged a fine beautiful pledge. > **""Order Bilal to call and Abu Bakr to lead the people. Bring a man I may lean upon.""**"
"8936","Abdullah ibn Masud, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that when the Messenger of Allah was taken the Ansar said, from us an amir and from you an amir. Umar came and said, O Ansar, do you not know that the Messenger ordered Abu Bakr to lead the people, which of you would willingly advance before Abu Bakr. They said, we seek refuge in Allah from advancing before Abu Bakr."
"8937","Abu al-Bakhtari reports that Umar said to Abu Ubaydah, stretch your hand that I may pledge you, for I heard the Messenger of Allah say. > **""You are the trustworthy one of this nation.""** Abu Ubaydah said, I would not advance before a man whom the Messenger ordered to lead us and who led us till he died."
"8938","Abu Said al-Khudri, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that when the Messenger died the orators of the Ansar stood saying, O Muhajirun, when the Messenger sent a man of you he joined a man of us, so we see this affair should have two men, one of us and one of you. Zayd ibn Thabit stood and said, the Messenger was of the Muhajirun and we were his Ansar, so we are Ansar of whoever stands in his place. Abu Bakr said, may Allah reward you O Ansar and make your speaker firm, by Allah had you said otherwise we would not have reconciled."
"8939","Isa ibn Atiyyah reports that Abu Bakr al-Siddiq stood the morrow after his pledge and addressed the people saying, O people I return your opinion to you, I am not the best of you, so pledge the best of you. They said, O Caliph of the Messenger of Allah, by Allah you are the best of us. He said, people entered Islam willingly and unwillingly, they are guests and neighbours of Allah, so if you can let Allah not seek you for His covenant then do. I have a devil that visits me, so if you see me answer me. Do not harm your hair and skins. Inspect the exactions of your learned. No flesh grown of unlawful shall enter Paradise. Watch me with your helpers, if I am upright follow me, if I deviate straighten me, if I obey Allah obey me, if I disobey Allah disobey me."
"8940","Qays ibn Abi Hazim reports that he sat with Abu Bakr al-Siddiq a month after the death of the Prophet, and it was announced prayer is gathering, the first such prayer among Muslims. People gathered and he ascended a minbar made for him, the first sermon in Islam. He praised Allah then said, O people I wish another sufficed me this, and if you take me by the practice of your Prophet I cannot bear it, for he was protected from Satan and revelation descended upon him from heaven."
"8941","Ibn Abi Mulaykah reports that it was said to Abu Bakr, O Caliph of Allah. He said, I am the caliph of the Messenger of Allah, and I am content with it."
"8942","Qays ibn Abi Hazim reports that he saw Umar with a palm stalk seating the people saying, hear and obey the caliph of the Messenger of Allah. Then a freedman of Abu Bakr called Sadid came with a document and read it, Abu Bakr says, hear and obey whoever is in this document, by Allah I have not spared you. Qays said, then I saw Umar after that upon the minbar."
"8943","Aishah, may Allah be pleased with her, reports that she was with the Prophet and he said, O Aishah, if only we had one to converse with us. She said, shall I send for Abu Bakr, and he fell silent. He repeated, shall I send for Umar, and he fell silent. Then he called a servant and whispered, and Uthman sought permission and entered, and the Prophet conversed privately long, then said. > **""O Uthman, Allah shall clothe you with a shirt, and if the hypocrites want you to remove it do not remove it, no honour in that.""** He said it twice or thrice."
"8944","Zayd ibn Aslam reports that Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, said to the six with whom the Messenger died pleased, pledge him whom Abdur Rahman ibn Awf pledges, and if any refuses strike his neck."
"8945","Abu Wail reports that he said to Abdur Rahman ibn Awf, how did you pledge Uthman and leave Ali. He said, what is my fault, I began with Ali and said, I pledge you upon the Book of Allah, the practice of His Messenger, and the conduct of Abu Bakr and Umar. He said, as much as I am able. Then I offered it to Uthman and he accepted."
"8946","Fadalah ibn Abi Fadalah, whose father was of Badr, reports that he went with his father visiting Ali in a heavy illness, and his father said, what keeps you in this dwelling, if your term comes none but Bedouin of Juhaynah will carry you to Madinah, but if it comes in Madinah your companions will care and pray over you. Ali said, the Messenger of Allah covenanted to me that I shall not die until I am appointed ruler, then this, meaning his beard, shall be dyed from this, meaning his head. He was killed and Abu Fadalah was killed with Ali at Siffin. > **""You shall not die until you are appointed ruler, then this beard shall be dyed from this head.""**"
"8947","Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said. > **""O Ali, if you take charge after me, expel the people of Najran from the Arabian Peninsula.""**"
"8948","Abdullah ibn Masud, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that he was with the Prophet on the night of the delegation of the jinn, and he breathed and he asked what is wrong. He said, my death has been announced to me O Ibn Masud. He said, appoint a successor. He said, whom. He said, Abu Bakr, and he fell silent. After a while he breathed again and said the same, he said Umar, and he fell silent. Again he breathed and he said Ali ibn Abi Talib. > **""My death has been announced to me. By Him in Whose Hand is my soul, if they obey him they shall all enter Paradise entirely.""**"
"8949","Abu Maymunah reports that Muawiyah ibn Abi Sufyan said, the people of Makkah expelled the Messenger of Allah so the caliphate shall not be among them, and the people of Madinah killed Uthman so the caliphate shall never return among them."
"8950","Abu Said al-Khudri, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that he heard the Messenger of Allah say, among you is one who shall fight for the interpretation of the Quran as I fought for its revelation. Abu Bakr asked, is it I, he said no. Umar asked, is it I, he said no, but it is the mender of the sandal, and he had given Ali his sandal to mend. > **""Among you is one who shall fight for the interpretation of the Quran as I fought for its revelation. It is the mender of the sandal.""**"
"8951","Ali ibn Rabiah reports that he heard Ali upon this minbar say, the Prophet covenanted to me to fight the breakers of pledges, the unjust deviators, and the seceders from religion."
"8952","Said ibn Amr ibn Said ibn al-As reports that Muawiyah took the water vessel after Abu Hurayrah to follow the Messenger, and Abu Hurayrah complained ill. While Muawiyah performed ablution for the Messenger he raised his head once or twice and said. > **""O Muawiyah, if you are given authority, fear Allah and be just.""** Muawiyah said, I ever thought I would be tried with office because of that saying until I was tried."
"8953","Al-Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that he was with the Prophet one night and he said, look, do you see a star in the sky. He said yes. He said, what do you see. He said, al-Thurayya. He said. > **""As many as its number shall rule this nation from your loins, O uncle, in tribulation.""**"
"8954","Abu Muawiyah reports that he had a narration by which he could earn the world but would not carry it to the ruler. His father asked what it is. He said, when Zayd revolted he came to his maternal aunt next morning saying Zayd has revolted. She said, the poor one shall be killed as his fathers were. He said, men of understanding went with him. She said, I was with Umm Salamah, wife of the Prophet, when they mentioned the caliphate and she said, they were with the Prophet and mentioned the caliphate after him saying the children of Fatimah. The Messenger said. > **""They shall never reach it, but it is in the children of my uncle and namesake of my father until they hand it to the Dajjal.""**"
"8955","Anas ibn Malik, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that no one of Banu Umayyah shall rule a year but a child of al-Abbas shall rule years. A sitter said, O Abu Hamzah, did the Messenger say it. He said, yes, as surely as you are here. > **""No one of Banu Umayyah shall rule a year but a child of al-Abbas shall rule years.""**"
"8956","Umm al-Fadl, may Allah be pleased with her, reports that she passed the Messenger sitting at al-Hijr and he said, O Umm al-Fadl, she answered. He said, you are pregnant with a boy. She said, how when Quraysh have sworn not to approach women. He said, it is as I say, and when you deliver bring him to me. When she delivered she brought him, he called adhan in his right ear and iqamah in his left, fed him of his saliva and named him Abdullah, then said, take away the father of the caliphs. She told al-Abbas, a handsome tall well-dressed man, who dressed and came to the Prophet. The Prophet rose, kissed between his eyes, seated him at his right and said, this is my uncle, let whoever wills boast of his uncle. Al-Abbas said, some saying O Messenger. He said, why should I not say, O uncle, while you are my uncle, remnant of my fathers, my heir and best of my family I leave behind. He asked about Umm al-Fadl's words. He said, it is after one hundred thirty-two, then among you al-Saffah, al-Mansur and al-Mahdi, and it remains in their children until the last of them prays with the Messiah Isa son of Maryam. > **""Look, do you see a star. You are pregnant with a boy. Take away the father of the caliphs. This is my uncle, let whoever wills boast of his uncle.""**"
"8957","Uqbah ibn Amir, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that he saw the Messenger take the hand of his uncle al-Abbas and say. > **""O Abbas, there is no prophethood but caliphate follows it. At the end of time seventeen from your children shall rule, among them al-Saffah, al-Mansur, al-Mahdi who is no Mahdi, al-Jamuh, al-Aqib, al-Wahin from your children. Woe to my nation from him, how he shall hamstring it, destroy it and consume its wealth, he and his followers upon other than Islam. When allegiance is given to his loins, at the eighteenth their state ends and the people of the west emerge from their homes.""**"
"8958","Abdullah ibn Masud, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that the Messenger said to al-Abbas. > **""O uncle, the world shall not pass until one of your children rules at the end of time at the end of their state, the eighteenth, with a blind deaf tribulation in which nine thousand nine hundred of every ten thousand are killed and few escape, their fighting in a place in Iraq.""** Al-Abbas wept and he said, what makes you weep, they are the worst of my nation who dart out of religion as the arrow darts from the target, seeking this world caring not for the Hereafter."
"8959","Nufayr ibn Malik reports that the Messenger of Allah said. > **""The children of al-Abbas shall not perish until the tribes of the Arabs rage against them, at their hardest with no helper in heaven nor excuser on earth. As if I see them upon their mules in Kufa and the veiled maiden in her chamber says, kill them, may Allah kill them, show them no mercy, may Allah show them no mercy, for long they showed us no mercy.""**"
"8960","Al-Numan ibn Bashir, may Allah be pleased with them both, reports that they sat in the mosque and Bashir was reticent, then Abu Thalabah al-Khushani asked, O Bashir ibn Sad, do you remember the narration about rulers. Hudhayfah said, I remember his sermon, and Abu Thalabah sat. Hudhayfah said, the Messenger of Allah said. > **""Prophethood shall be among you as long as Allah wills, then He lifts it when He wills. Then caliphate upon the method of prophethood as long as Allah wills, then He lifts it. Then biting kingship as long as Allah wills, then He lifts it. Then tyrannical kingship as long as Allah wills, then He lifts it. Then caliphate upon the method of prophethood.""** Then he fell silent. Habib said, when Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz rose and Yazid ibn al-Numan was among his companions, he wrote this narration reminding him hoping the Commander of the Believers after the biting and tyrannical kingship is Umar, and Umar was pleased."
"8961","Abu Thalabah al-Khushani, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that Muadh ibn Jabal and Abu Ubaydah whispered and he said, have you not remembered the bequest of the Messenger who entrusted you with me. They said, we only recalled a narration he told us. > **""This affair began as prophethood and mercy, then shall be caliphate and mercy, then biting kingship, then insolence and tyranny and corruption in the nation. They shall permit silk, wine, private parts and corruption in the nation, and shall be helped and provided upon that until they meet Allah.""**"
"8962","Al-Tabarani reports from Muadh and Abu Ubaydah that the Messenger said similar to Abu Yala's narration adding, they shall permit silk, private parts and wines. > **""They shall permit silk, private parts and wines.""**"
"8963","Abu Thalabah al-Khushani, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that he met the Messenger and asked, entrust me to a man of good teaching, and he entrusted him to Abu Ubaydah ibn al-Jarrah saying, I entrust you to one who teaches and disciplines well. He came while Abu Ubaydah and Bashir ibn Sad conversed and fell silent on seeing him. He said, by Allah this is not as the Messenger told me. He said, sit till we tell you. > **""Among you is prophethood, then caliphate upon the method of prophethood, then kingship and tyranny.""**"
"8964","Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, reports that the Messenger of Allah said. > **""The first of this affair is prophethood and mercy, then caliphate and mercy, then kingship and mercy, then command and mercy. Then they shall jostle over it as donkeys jostle. Upon you is jihad, the best of your jihad is guarding the frontier, and the best of your guarding is Asqalan.""**"
"8965","Qays ibn Jabir al-Sadafi from his father from his grandfather reports that the Messenger of Allah said. > **""There shall be after me caliphs, after the caliphs princes, after the princes kings, after the kings tyrants. Then a man of my household shall emerge filling the earth with justice as it was filled with injustice. Then the Qahtani shall be appointed, and by Him who sent me with truth he is no less than him.""**"
"8966","Muadh ibn Jabal, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that the Messenger of Allah said. > **""Thirty years prophethood, and thirty years kingship and tyranny, and no good in what is beyond that.""**"
"8967","Masruq reports that they sat with Abdullah while he taught Quran, and a man asked, O Abu Abd al-Rahman, did you ask the Messenger how many caliphs shall rule this nation. Abdullah said, none asked me since I came to Iraq before you, yes we asked the Messenger and he said. > **""Twelve, like the number of the chiefs of the Children of Israel.""**"
"8968","Abu Juhayfah, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that he was with his uncle at the Prophet while he preached saying, the affair of my nation shall remain sound until twelve caliphs pass, and he lowered his voice. He asked his uncle before him what he said, he said. > **""The affair of my nation shall remain sound until twelve caliphs pass. All of them from Quraysh.""**"
"8969","Abdullah ibn Amr ibn al-As, may Allah be pleased with them both, reports that the Messenger of Allah said. > **""When twelve of Bani Murrah ibn Kab rule, hatred and hypocrisy shall last till the Hour.""**"
"8970","Jabir ibn Samurah, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that he heard the Messenger preaching on the minbar say. > **""Twelve custodians of Quraysh, the enmity of whoever opposes them shall not harm them.""** He turned behind and Umar ibn al-Khattab among people confirmed the narration as he heard."
"8971","In a version, this affair shall remain, with Rawh ibn Ata who is weak. > **""This affair shall remain.""**"
"8972","Al-Bazzar reports from Jabir ibn Samurah alone adding that the Prophet returned home and he asked, what then, he said. > **""Then shall be killing and chaos.""**"
"8973","Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman reports that the Messenger died while Abu Bakr was in a district of Madinah. He came, uncovered his face, kissed him and said, may my father and mother be for you, how pure alive and dead, Muhammad has died by the Lord of the Kabah. Then Abu Bakr and Umar set out till they reached them, and Abu Bakr spoke omitting nothing revealed in Quran or mentioned by the Messenger concerning them. They said, you know the Messenger said, had people take a valley and the Ansar a valley I would take the valley of the Ansar. And you know O Sad, while you sat, the Messenger said, Quraysh are guardians of this affair, the righteous of people follow their righteous and the wicked follow their wicked. Sad said, you spoke truth, we are ministers and you are princes. > **""Had people take a valley and the Ansar take a valley, I would take the valley of the Ansar. Quraysh are guardians of this affair.""**"
"8974","Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that his ears heard and his heart retained from the Messenger of Allah. > **""People follow Quraysh, their righteous follow their righteous and their wicked follow their wicked.""**"
"8975","Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that the Messenger addressed the people one day saying. > **""Verily rulers are from Quraysh, verily rulers are from Quraysh, verily rulers are from Quraysh, as long as they uphold three: when they judge they are just, when they covenant they fulfill, when mercy is sought they show mercy. Whoever of them does not do that, upon him is the curse of Allah, the angels and all people.""**"
"8976","Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that the Messenger of Allah said. > **""The leaders are from Quraysh. Their righteous are rulers of their righteous, and their wicked are rulers of their wicked. Each has a right, so give each rightful his right. Even if a mutilated Abyssinian slave is appointed over you, hear and obey him, unless one of you is given choice between his Islam and striking of his neck. If he is given choice between his Islam and striking of his neck, let him stretch his neck, may his mother weep, for no world nor Hereafter remains after loss of his religion.""**"
"8977","Abdullah ibn Masud, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that they were near eighty men of Quraysh with the Messenger, none but Qurashi, and he never saw more beautiful faces. They mentioned women till he wished silence. He came and testified then said. > **""O assembly of Quraysh, you are guardians of this affair as long as you do not disobey Allah. When you disobey Him He shall send upon you one who peels you as this stick is peeled.""** For a stick in his hand, then he peeled it till white and smooth."
"8978","Bukayr ibn Wahb al-Jazari reports that Anas said, shall I tell you a narration I do not tell everyone. The Messenger stood at the door of the house while they were inside and said. > **""The leaders are from Quraysh. I have a right over you, and they have a like right over you, as long as when mercy is sought they show mercy, when they covenant they fulfill, when they judge they are just. Whoever of them does not do that, upon him is the curse of Allah, the angels and all people.""** In a version al-Bazzar said kingship is in Quraysh."
"8979","Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that the Messenger of Allah said. > **""I have a right over Quraysh, and Quraysh have a right over you, as long as they judge justly, when entrusted they discharge, when mercy is sought they show mercy.""**"
"8980","Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that the Messenger said to al-Abbas. > **""Among you are prophethood and kingdom.""**"
"8981","Sayyar ibn Salamah Abu al-Minhal reports that he entered with his father upon Abu Barzah while as a boy with earrings in his ears, and he said the Messenger said. > **""Rulers are from Quraysh, rulers are from Quraysh, rulers are from Quraysh, as long as they do three: when they judge they are just, when mercy is sought they show mercy, when they covenant they fulfill. Whoever of them does not do that, upon him is the curse of Allah, the angels and all people.""**"
"8982","Abu Masud al-Ansari, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to Quraysh. > **""This affair is among you and you are its guardians until you innovate deeds. When you do that Allah shall set over you the worst of His creation who shall peel you as the stick is peeled.""**"
"8983","Abu Musa, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that the Messenger stood at the door of a house with Quraysh inside, holding the doorposts, asking if any but Qurashi is inside. They said only the son of our sister, and he said the nephew of a people is of them, then said. > **""The son of the sister of a people is of them. This affair is in Quraysh as long as when mercy is sought they show mercy, when they judge they are just, when they distribute they are equitable. Whoever of them does not do that, upon him is the curse of Allah, the angels and all people. None of his obligatory or voluntary deed is accepted.""**"
"8984","Dhu Mikhbar, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that the Messenger of Allah said. > **""This affair was in Himyar, then Allah removed it from them and placed it in Quraysh, and it shall return to them.""**"
"8985","Shurayh ibn Ubayd reports from Jubayr ibn Nufayr, Kathir ibn Murrah, Amr ibn al-Aswad, al-Miqdam ibn Madikarib and Abu Umamah that a man came to the Prophet asking if rule is only in his people, he said yes. He asked to enjoin them regarding us, so he said to Quraysh, I warn you by Allah lest you burden my nation after me, then said to the people. > **""I warn you by Allah lest you burden my nation after me. There shall be rulers after me, so render them their obedience, for the ruler is like a shield to be shielded with. If they are righteous and Godfearing and command you to good it is well, and if they do evil and command you to it, it is upon them and you are free of it.""**"
"8986","Amr ibn Awf al-Muzani, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that the Messenger sat with them then entered his house saying none but Qurashi shall enter upon me. He asked if any not of them is with them, they said a nephew and a freedman, and he said the ally and nephew are of them, then enjoined Quraysh with unity and verses, and mercy for the Ansar. > **""The ally of a people is of them and the nephew of a people is of them. O assembly of Quraysh, you are guardians after me of this affair, so die not but as Muslims. Hold to the rope of Allah all together and be not divided. Be not as those who divided after clear proofs came. O assembly of Quraysh, preserve me in my Companions and their sons and sons of sons. May Allah have mercy on the Ansar and sons of the Ansar and sons of sons of the Ansar.""**"
"8987","Abu Said al-Khudri, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that the Messenger stood over a house of Quraysh holding the doorposts asking if any but Qurashi is inside, they said only our nephew, and he said the nephew is of them, then said. > **""The nephew of a people is of them. This affair is in Quraysh as long as when mercy is sought they show mercy, when they judge they are just, when they distribute they are equitable. Whoever of them does not do that, upon him is the curse of Allah, the angels and all people.""**"
"8988","Anas ibn Malik, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that they were in a house of Muhajirun and Ansar when the Messenger came and each made room hoping he sits beside him, but he stood at the door holding its posts and said. > **""The leaders are from Quraysh, and I have a great right over you, and they have the like as long as they do three: when mercy is sought they show mercy, when they judge they are just, when they covenant they fulfill. Whoever of them does not do that, upon him is the curse of Allah, the angels and all people.""** In a version, when entrusted they discharge."
"8989","Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, reports that the Messenger of Allah said. > **""The safety of earth people from drowning is the bow, and the safety of earth people from division is loyalty to Quraysh. Quraysh are the people of Allah. When any Arab tribe opposes them they become the party of Iblis.""** In a version, safety of my nation from division, and Quraysh are the people of Allah thrice."
"8990","Sahl ibn Sad, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that the Prophet said. > **""People follow Quraysh in good and evil.""**"
"8991","Al-Harith ibn al-Harith, Kathir ibn Murrah, Amr ibn al-Aswad and Abu Umamah, may Allah be pleased with them, report that the Prophet said. > **""The best leaders of Quraysh are the best leaders of the people.""**"
"8992","Muawiyah ibn Abi Sufyan, may Allah be pleased with him, reports while on the minbar that al-Dahhak ibn Qays, just in himself, told him the Messenger said. > **""A governor from Quraysh shall ever remain.""**"
"8993","Abdullah ibn Hantab, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that the Messenger addressed them at al-Juhfah asking, am I not more worthy of you than yourselves, they said yes. He said, I ask you of two, the Quran and my kin. Do not advance before Quraysh lest you stray, nor lag behind them lest you perish, nor teach them for they know more than you. The strength of a Qurashi man exceeds two others. Were Quraysh not to exult I would tell what they have with Allah. The best of Quraysh are the best of people. > **""Am I not more worthy of you than yourselves. I ask you of the Quran and my kin. Advance not before Quraysh lest you stray, lag not behind them lest you perish. The best of Quraysh are the best of people.""**"
"8994","Thawban, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that the Messenger of Allah said. > **""Be upright to Quraysh as long as they are upright to you. If you do not, place your swords on your shoulders and annihilate their green. If you do not, be then wretched farmers eating from toil of your hands.""**"
"8995","Al-Ahnaf ibn Qays reports that he heard Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, say no Qurashi enters a door but people enter with him, and he knew not its meaning till Umar was stabbed and ordered Suhayb to lead three days and food for the days of consultation. When they returned from the funeral tables were laid but people abstained in grief, then al-Abbas ibn Abd al-Muttalib said, O people the Messenger died and we ate and drank after him, and Abu Bakr died and we ate and drank. O people eat of this food. He stretched his hand and they ate, and he understood his saying."
"8996","Utbah ibn Abd, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that the Prophet said the caliphate is in Quraysh, and the narration was mentioned before in the Book of Rulings. > **""The caliphate is in Quraysh.""**"
"8997","Abdullah ibn Amr, may Allah be pleased with them both, reports that the Messenger of Allah said. > **""In Paradise is a palace called Adn, around it towers and chambers, with five thousand doors, at each door five thousand chosen ones. None enters or dwells it but a prophet, a truthful one, a martyr, or a just imam.""**"
"8998","Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, reports that the Prophet said the sultan is the shade of Allah on earth to whom every wronged servant resorts. If he is just he has reward and upon subjects is thanks, if unjust or oppressive the burden is upon him and upon subjects is patience. When rulers are fought the sky withholds, when zakah is withheld cattle perish, when adultery appears poverty appears, when covenant is betrayed disbelievers prevail. > **""The sultan is the shade of Allah on earth to whom every wronged of His servants resorts. If he is just he has reward, and if he is unjust the burden is upon him and patience upon the subjects.""**"
"8999","Maqil ibn Yasar, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that the Messenger of Allah said. > **""Injustice shall not linger after me but little till it rises, and whenever injustice rises the like of justice departs, till one born in injustice knows nothing else. Then Allah shall bring justice, and whenever justice comes the like of injustice departs, till one born in justice knows nothing else.""**"
"9000","Anas ibn Malik, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that the Prophet said. > **""This nation shall ever be well as long as when they speak they are truthful, when they judge they are just, when mercy is sought they show mercy.""**"
"9001","Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that the Messenger of Allah said. > **""When you judge be just, and when you kill do well, for Allah is Good and loves the good-doers.""**"
"9002","Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, reports that the Messenger of Allah said. > **""A day of a just imam is better than worship of sixty years, and a hadd established on earth in its right is purer therein than rain of forty years.""**"
"9003","Abu Qahdham reports that in the time of Ziyad a purse was found with date-stone-like things inscribed, this grew in a time when justice was practiced."
"9004","Abu Said, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that the Messenger of Allah said. > **""The severest of people in punishment on the Day of Resurrection is an unjust imam.""**"
"9005","Abu Musa, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that the Messenger of Allah said. > **""In Hell is a valley, in the valley a well called Habhab. It is binding upon Allah to lodge every obstinate tyrant therein.""**"
"9006","Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that the Prophet said the best of people in rank with Allah on Resurrection is a just gentle imam, and the worst of Allah's servants in rank is an unjust harsh imam. > **""The best of people in rank with Allah on the Day of Resurrection is a just gentle imam, and the worst is an unjust harsh imam.""**"
"9007","Abdullah ibn Saba reports that it was said to Ali, will you not appoint a successor. He said, no, but I leave you to what the Messenger left you to."
"9008","Al-Agharr Abu Malik reports that when Abu Bakr wished to appoint Umar he summoned him and said, I call you to a wearying affair for its bearer. Fear Allah O Umar by obedience and obey Him by piety, for piety is guarded. The affair is presented, none deserves it but who acts by it. Who commands truth but acts falsehood, commands good but acts evil, his hope shall soon sever and his deed be void. If you rule them, keep your hands dry of their blood, your belly lean of their wealth, your tongue dry of their honours, and no strength but by Allah."
"9009","Muhammad ibn Sirin reports that when Muawiyah took pledge for Yazid he performed Hajj passing Madinah and addressed the people, we have pledged Yazid so pledge him. Al-Husayn ibn Ali stood saying, by Allah I am worthier of it than he, my father better than his father, my grandfather better than his grandfather, my mother better than his mother, and I better than he. Muawiyah answered, as to your grandfather better than his, true, the Messenger better than Abu Sufyan. As to your mother better than his, true, Fatimah better than the daughter of Mujaddal. As to your father better than his, your father contended with his and Allah decreed for his over yours. As to you better than he, he is more cunning and wiser than you, I would not delight in a thousand like you for him."
"9010","Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that the Prophet said. > **""When pledge is given to two caliphs, kill the latter of them.""**"
"9011","Said ibn Jubayr reports that Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr said to Muawiyah in their dispute over Yazid's pledge, O Muawiyah, you told me the Messenger said. > **""When there are two caliphs on earth, kill the latter of them.""**"
"9012","Ibn Abi Mulaykah reports that it was said to Abu Bakr, O Caliph of Allah. He said, I am the caliph of the Messenger of Allah, and I am content with it, and I am content with it."
"9013","Al-Zuhri reports that Uthman ibn Hunayf greeted Muawiyah with Syrians present saying, peace upon you O Amir. They asked, who is this hypocrite who shortened the title of Amir al-Muminin. Uthman said to Muawiyah, they blame me for what you know better, for I greeted Abu Bakr, Umar and Uthman with it. Muawiyah said, I think it was as you say, but Syrians since the tribulation say, by Allah we know our religion and shorten not greeting of our caliph, and I think you Medinans call the charity collector amir."
"9014","Abdullah ibn Amr, may Allah be pleased with them both, reports that Hamzah ibn Abd al-Muttalib came to the Messenger saying, O Messenger of Allah, place me over something to live by. The Messenger said, O Hamzah, is a soul you give life to dearer to you or a soul you kill. He said, a soul I give life to. He said, upon you is your own soul. > **""O Hamzah, is a soul you give life to dearer to you or a soul you kill. Upon you is your own soul.""**"
"9015","Hibban ibn Buh al-Sudai reports that his people disbelieved and he heard the Prophet prepared an army to them, so he came saying his people are upon Islam. He asked, is it so, he said yes. He followed him till dawn, called adhan, was given a vessel, the Prophet placed fingers therein and springs burst, saying whoever wishes ablution let him perform. He prayed and was appointed over them with their charity. A man complained of injustice and the Prophet said, no good in leadership for a Muslim. Then a beggar asked charity and he said charity is headache and burning in belly, so he returned his document of command and charity asking how to accept after hearing that, and he said, it is as you heard. > **""Is it so. Whoever wishes ablution let him perform. No good in leadership for a Muslim. Charity is headache in the head and burning in the belly.""**"
"9016","Aishah, may Allah be pleased with her, reports that she heard the Messenger say. > **""Woe to the rulers, woe to the overseers, woe to the trustees. A day shall come upon one when he wishes he hung from a star and never held office.""**"
"9017","Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that the Prophet said. > **""Woe to the rulers, woe to the overseers, woe to the trustees. Peoples on Resurrection shall wish their forelocks hung by Thurayya swaying between heaven and earth and they never held anything.""**"
"9018","Rafi al-Tai, companion of Abu Bakr in Dhat al-Salasil, reports that he asked him of their pledge, and he told of the Ansar's speech and his speech to them and Umar's speech reminding of his leading them by the Messenger's order in illness, so they pledged him for that and he accepted fearing tribulation followed by apostasy."
"9019","Yazid ibn Mawhab reports that Uthman said to Ibn Umar, judge among people. He said, I shall not judge between two nor lead two, did you not hear the Messenger say, whoever seeks refuge in Allah has sought mighty refuge. He said yes. He said, I seek refuge in Allah from your employing me, so he excused him saying, tell none. > **""Whoever seeks refuge in Allah has sought mighty refuge.""**"
"9020","Zayd ibn Thabit, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that he said before the Prophet, evil is leadership, and the Prophet said. > **""Good is leadership for one who takes it in its right and lawful, and evil is leadership for one who takes it without its right. It shall be regret on Resurrection.""**"
"9021","Shaddad ibn Aws, brother of Hassan and conqueror of Iliya for Muawiyah, reports while reviewing Muawiyah that he heard the Messenger mention leadership saying. > **""Its first is blame, its second regret, its third punishment from Allah on Resurrection, except one who shows mercy and is just and gives wealth thus and thus with his hand.""** Then he fell silent as Allah willed then said, how can justice be with kin."
"9022","Awf ibn Malik, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that the Messenger said, shall I tell you of leadership and what it is. He called thrice in loudest voice, what is it O Messenger. He said. > **""If you wish I tell you of leadership and what it is. Its first is blame, its second regret, its third punishment on Resurrection except one who is just. And how can he be just with his kin.""**"
"9023","Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, reports, Sharik doubted its raising, that leadership is first regret, middle fine, last punishment on Resurrection."
"9024","Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that the Messenger employed al-Miqdad ibn al-Aswad al-Kindi over a cavalry detachment, and on return asked how he found it. He said he saw them exalting and acting till he thought himself not so, and the Prophet said, it is so. Al-Miqdad swore by Him who sent him with truth never to work an office again, and they would ask him to lead prayer and he refused. > **""How did you find it. It is so.""**"
"9025","Al-Miqdad ibn al-Aswad, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that the Messenger sent him on a mission and on return asked how he finds himself. He said he ever thought servants were with him, and by Allah he shall never command even two men after it. > **""How do you find yourself.""**"
"9026","Malik ibn al-Harith reports from a man, in Abu Kurayb's book from Humayd from a man, that the Prophet employed a man over a detachment, and on return asked how he found command. He said he was as the folk, when he inclined they inclined, when he halted they halted. The Prophet said, the bearer of authority is at the gate of reproach except whom Allah protects. The man swore never to work for him or another, and the Prophet laughed till his molars appeared. > **""How did you find command. The bearer of authority is at the gate of reproach except whom Allah protects.""**"
"9027","Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, reports that the Messenger employed a man over a work who said, O Messenger choose for me. He said, stay in your house. > **""Stay in your house.""**"
"9028","Ismah, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that the Messenger employed a man over charity who said, O Messenger choose for me. He said, sit in your house. > **""Sit in your house.""**"
"9029","Rafi ibn Amr al-Tai, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that the Messenger sent Amr ibn al-As over Dhat al-Salasil with Abu Bakr, Umar and chief Companions till they camped at the mountains of Tayy, and Amr sought a guide known only as Rafi ibn Amr the thief raider. After the campaign he asked Abu Bakr for something to be of them, and he taught five on fingers: testimony, prayer, zakah if wealth, Hajj, fasting Ramadan, and another, command not even two. He asked, is command but among you Badr folk. He said, soon it shall spread to you and below, for when the Prophet was sent people entered Islam, some guided, some by sword, guests and neighbours of Allah. When a ruler lets people wrong one another and takes not for some from some, Allah avenges him. A man's neighbour's sheep is taken and he burns in anger for him, and Allah behind him. After a year Abu Bakr was made successor and he reminded him, you forbade command yet rode greatest of Muhammad's nation. He said yes, whoever establishes not Allah's Book among them, upon him is the curse of Allah. > **""Bear witness there is no god but Allah and Muhammad is His servant and Messenger, establish prayer, give zakah, perform Hajj, fast Ramadan. Command not even two. Whoever establishes not Allah's Book among them, upon him is the curse of Allah.""**"
"9030","Abdur Rahman ibn Awf, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that he visited Abu Bakr in his fatal illness asking how he is, and he sat upright praising Allah well, yet in pain burdened with their charge, having covenanted after him choosing their best while each coveted it. He saw the world advancing with silk curtains and brocade and woollen beds as thorns of sadan, and by Allah one's neck struck without hadd is better than plunging in worldliness. He regretted three done wishing undone: uncovering Fatimah's house, closing upon war, casting the affair at Saqifah upon Abu Ubaydah or Umar while minister. He regretted three undone wishing done: striking al-Ashath captive, sparing al-Fujah al-Sulami, sending Umar to Iraq with Khalid to Sham. He regretted three unasked of the Messenger: in whom is this affair that none dispute its folk, have Ansar a share therein, and the paternal aunt and brother's daughter of which he had need."
"9031","Ziyad ibn al-Harith al-Sudai, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that he pledged the Prophet and hearing he would send an army to his folk guaranteed their Islam and obedience. He wrote them and a delegation came. He asked, O brother of Suda, are you obeyed among them, he said rather Allah guided them. He said, shall I appoint you over them, he said yes, and wrote it granting their charity. On a journey he stayed with him alone till dawn, he called adhan, was asked for water little not sufficing, poured in a vessel, the Prophet placed his hand and springs flowed between fingers saying, O brother of Suda, were I not shy of my Lord we would drink and water. Call who wishes ablution. Bilal came to iqamah and he said, the brother of Suda called, and who calls makes iqamah. After Fajr locals complained of their agent's pre-Islamic grudge, and he told Companions, no good in leadership for a believing man. It entered his heart, and a beggar asked and he said begging in richness is headache, so he returned his paper. The Prophet accepted, and part is in the Sunan. > **""O brother of Suda, are you obeyed among your folk. Pour it in the vessel. The brother of Suda called, and who calls makes iqamah. No good in leadership for a believing man.""**"
"9032","Nafi reports that when Uthman was killed Ali came to Ibn Umar saying, you are beloved among people, so go to Sham. Ibn Umar said by kinship and companionship to the Messenger and womb between us, and he did not repeat."
"9033","Abu Umamah, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that the Prophet said. > **""No man rules ten or more but comes to Allah on Resurrection shackled hand to neck, his righteousness freeing him or his sin binding him. Its first is blame, middle regret, last disgrace on Resurrection.""**"
"9034","Ubadah ibn al-Samit, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that the Messenger of Allah said. > **""No ruler of ten but brought on Resurrection with hand shackled to neck till truth frees him or binds him. Who learns Quran then forgets it meets Allah leprous.""**"
"9035","A man reports from Sad ibn Ubadah, may Allah be pleased with him, heard more than once or twice, that the Messenger said. > **""No ruler of ten but brought on Resurrection shackled, none freeing him from that shackle but justice.""**"
"9036","Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that the Prophet said. > **""No ruler of ten but brought on Resurrection shackled till justice frees him or injustice binds him.""**"
"9037","In a version, if he was evil his shackle is increased, reported by al-Bazzar and al-Tabarani in al-Awsat. > **""If he was evil his shackle is increased unto his shackle.""**"
"9038","In al-Tabarani's al-Awsat version, Allah pardons whom He wills or punishes whom He wills. > **""Allah pardons him as He wills or punishes him as He wills.""**"
"9039","Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that the Prophet said. > **""The unjust imam shall be brought on Resurrection and the subjects dispute him and prevail, and it is said to him, fill a pillar of Hell's pillars.""**"
"9040","Abu Wail Shaqiq ibn Salamah reports that Umar employed Bishr ibn Asim over Hawazin charities and he lagged. Umar asked, is not hearing and obedience ours, he said yes, but he heard the Messenger say, whoever rules anything of Muslims is brought on Resurrection till stood upon the bridge of Hell, if good he is saved, if evil the bridge splits and he falls seventy autumns. Umar went out grieved and Abu Dharr met him asking why, and Umar told. Abu Dharr asked, did you not hear it from the Messenger, he said no. Abu Dharr bore witness he heard the Messenger say, whoever rules anyone is brought till stood upon the bridge dark and black, if good saved, if evil split and falls seventy autumns. Which narration pains your heart more, he said both pained, who can bear it. Abu Dharr said, one whose nose Allah cuts and cheek dusts, we know but good, and if you appoint one unjust he may not escape its sin. > **""Whoever rules anything of the Muslims is brought on the Day of Resurrection till stood upon the bridge of Hell. If he was good he is saved, and if evil the bridge splits with him and he falls therein seventy autumns.""**"
"9041","Qays ibn Asim reports from his father that Umar ibn al-Khattab sent him to aid in charity and he refused, saying he heard the Messenger say, on Resurrection the governor is ordered and stood upon Hell's bridge, Allah orders the bridge to shake removing every bone from place, then orders bones to return, then asks. If obedient to Allah He rescues and gives two shares of reward, if disobedient the bridge splits and he falls in Hell seventy autumns. Similar narrations precede in Rulings. > **""On the Day of Resurrection the governor is ordered and stood upon the bridge of Hell, and the bridge shakes removing every bone. If obedient to Allah He rescues him, and if disobedient he falls seventy autumns.""**"
"9042","Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, reports in raised form that the Messenger said. > **""No man rules ten but brought on Resurrection with hand shackled to neck till judgment between him and them.""**"
"9043","Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, reports that the Messenger said, whoever rules ten judging between them as they love or hate is brought on Resurrection with hand shackled to neck. If he judged by what Allah revealed, was not partial nor bribed, his right is freed. A sitter of Ata asked, O Abu Muhammad, must there be a shackle, he said yes by this Building, pointing to the Kabah. > **""Whoever rules ten and judges between them as they love or hate is brought on Resurrection with hand shackled to neck. If he judged by what Allah revealed and was not bribed, his right is freed.""**"
"9044","Abu al-Darda, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that he heard the Messenger say. > **""No governor of three but meets Allah with right shackled, his justice freeing him or his injustice binding him.""**"
"9045","Buraydah, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that the Messenger said. > **""No ruler of ten but comes to Allah on Resurrection with hand shackled to neck. If good he is freed, if evil his shackle is increased.""**"
"9046","Thawban, freedman of the Messenger, may Allah be pleased with him, said, perhaps your term is prolonged till you rule ten when people dwell villages, so beware ruling ten or more, for none stood over ten but comes to Allah with hand shackled to neck, nothing freeing but justice if just among them. And settle not villages, for settler of villages is as settler of graves."
"9047","Anas ibn Malik, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that the Messenger said, each of you is a shepherd responsible for his flock. The ruler is shepherd over people, the man over his household and wife and owned, the woman over husband's house and child, the slave over master's wealth. Each is shepherd responsible, so prepare answers to questions. They asked, O Messenger, what is its answer, he said deeds of righteousness. > **""Each of you is a shepherd and each responsible for his flock. The ruler is a shepherd over people responsible for them, the man over his household, the woman over her husband's house and child, the slave over his master's wealth. Prepare answers to questions. Deeds of righteousness.""**"
"9048","Aishah, may Allah be pleased with her, reports that the Prophet said. > **""Each of you is a shepherd and responsible.""**"
"9049","Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that the Messenger said. > **""No shepherd entrusted a flock but asked on Resurrection, did he uphold Allah's order therein or waste it.""**"
"9050","Abu Lubabah ibn Abd al-Mundhir, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that the Messenger forbade killing house snakes and said, each of you shepherd responsible, the ruler over people, the man over family, the wife over husband's house, the servant over master's wealth. Verily each shepherd responsible. Part in Sahih is only the prohibition. > **""Each of you is a shepherd responsible for his flock. The ruler over people is a shepherd responsible, the man over his family, the wife over her husband's house, the servant over his master's wealth. Verily each of you is a shepherd and responsible.""**"
"9051","Al-Miqdam, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that he heard the Messenger say. > **""No man over a people but comes on Resurrection preceding them with a banner he carries and they follow him. He is asked of them and they of him.""**"
"9052","Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, reports that the Messenger said. > **""No ruler appointed over ten but asked of them on Resurrection.""**"
"9053","Qatadah reports that Ibn Masud, may Allah be pleased with him, said, Allah shall ask every guardian of his charge, did he uphold Allah's order or waste it, till a man is asked of his household. Qatadah heard not from Ibn Masud."
"9054","Buraydah, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that the Messenger asked Jafar on return from Abyssinia what most amazed him. He said, a woman bearing a food basket on her head, a horseman knocked it scattering her food, she sat gathering then turned saying, woe to you when the King sets His Throne and takes for wronged from wrongdoer. The Messenger confirming her said. > **""No nation is sanctified, or how is a nation sanctified, whose weak cannot take his right from the strong without distress.""**"
"9055","Jabir, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that when Jafar came from Abyssinia the Messenger met him, and Jafar blushed in awe, so the Messenger kissed between his eyes saying, O beloved, you most resemble me in character and form, created of the clay I was created of. O beloved tell me of Abyssinian wonders. He said, by my father and mother, as I stood in a road an old woman with a basket on her head was pushed by a youth racing a horse dropping it, she stood straight following him with sight saying, woe to you tomorrow when the King sits on His Throne and requites wronged from wrongdoer. Jabir said, he saw the Messenger say. > **""O beloved, you most resemble me in character and form. Allah shall not sanctify a nation where the wronged cannot take his right from the wrongdoer without distress.""**"
"9056","Aishah, may Allah be pleased with her, reports that Ibn Masud wished to build a house and Quraysh said, shall we prevent Ibn Umm Abd building among us. The Messenger said, shall I command that while unjust, or I am unjust. Allah sanctifies no nation where the weak's right is not taken from the strong. Similar of Ibn Masud passed in Rulings. > **""Shall I command that while I am unjust. Allah sanctifies no nation where the right of its weak is not taken from its strong.""**"
"9057","Muawiyah, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said. > **""Allah shall not sanctify a nation where truth is not judged and the weak cannot take his right from the strong without distress.""**"
"9058","Rabiah ibn Yazid reports that Muawiyah wrote to Maslamah ibn Mukhallad to ask Abdullah ibn Amr ibn al-As whether he heard the Messenger say, no sanctified nation whose weak cannot take his right from its strong without compulsion. If yes, send by post. He said yes, so he sent from Egypt to Sham, and Muawiyah said, I too heard it but wished verification. > **""No sanctified nation whose weak cannot take his right from its strong without compulsion.""**"
"9059","Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, reports that the Messenger of Allah said. > **""The weak imam is cursed.""**"
"9060","Jabir ibn Samurah, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that the Messenger of Allah said. > **""Never shall succeed a people whose affair is ruled by a woman.""**"
"9061","Abdullah ibn al-Hajna reports that when Aishah, wife of the Prophet, came, they went to Abu Bakrah saying, here is Aishah come, go out with us. He said, I remembered a narration heard from the Messenger mentioning Bilqis of Saba. > **""Allah shall not sanctify a nation led by a woman.""**"
"9062","Al-Qasim reports that Abdullah said, when a ruler is appointed he has two inner circles of his folk, one commanding obedience of Allah and one commanding His disobedience, and he is with whichever of them he obeys. Al-Qasim did not meet Ibn Masud."
"9063","Aishah, may Allah be pleased with her, reports that the Messenger of Allah said. > **""Whomever Allah places over any affair of the Muslims intending good for him, He gives him a truthful minister. If he forgets he reminds him, and if he remembers he aids him.""**"
"9064","Abu al-Darda, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that he heard the Messenger say. > **""Whoever conveys to a sultan the need of one unable to convey it, Allah shall make his feet firm on the Bridge on a day feet slip.""**"
"9065","Muadh ibn Jabal, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that the Messenger of Allah said. > **""Whoever rules anything of the people then veils himself from the weak and needy, Allah shall veil Himself from him on Resurrection.""**"
"9066","Abu al-Sammah al-Azdi reports from a cousin of his among Companions who came to Muawiyah saying he heard the Messenger say. > **""Whoever rules the people then closes his door upon the poor, wronged and needy, Allah shall close doors of His mercy upon his need when neediest thereof.""**"
"9067","Abu Juhayfah, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that Muawiyah dispatched a mission and Abu al-Dahdah returned. Muawiyah asked, had you not gone out. He said yes, but I heard from the Messenger a narration I wish to place with you fearing not to meet you. > **""O people, whoever holds office then shuts his door upon the needy Muslims, Allah shall bar him entering Paradise's gate. Whoever's concern is this world, Allah forbids him my neighbourhood. I was sent with ruin of this world, not its building.""**"
"9068","Abu Firas reports that Umar ibn al-Khattab addressed the people saying, a time came when I thought whoever reads Quran intends Allah, then it seemed men read it intending what people have. So intend Allah in recitation and deeds. Beat not Muslims humiliating them, detain not in armies trialing them, lodge not in thickets wasting them, withhold not their rights driving them to ingratitude. Part in Sahih."
"9069","Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, reports that the Messenger of Allah said. > **""No one of my nation rules anything of the people and guards them not as he guards himself and family but shall not find fragrance of Paradise.""**"
"9070","Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, reports that the Prophet said. > **""Whoever rules anything of the Muslims, Allah shall not look to his need till he looks to their needs.""**"
"9071","Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, reports that the Messenger said, whoever aids falsehood to refute truth is free of Allah's and His Messenger's covenant. Whoever walks to Allah's sultan on earth to humiliate him, Allah humiliates him with stored disgrace on Resurrection. Allah's sultan on earth is His Book and His Prophet's practice. Whoever rules Muslims then employs one knowing a worthier knower of Book and Sunnah among them betrays Allah, His Messenger and believers. Whoever neglects people's needs, Allah neglects his till he attends theirs and pays their right. Whoever eats a dirham of riba, it is thirty-three adulteries. Flesh grown of unlawful, Fire worthier of it. > **""Whoever aids falsehood to refute truth is free of Allah's and His Messenger's covenant. Whoever rules then employs one knowing a worthier knower of Book and Sunnah betrays Allah, His Messenger and all believers. Flesh grown of unlawful, Fire is worthier of it.""**"
"9072","Al-Hasan reports that Ubaydullah ibn Ziyad came as ruler appointed by Muawiyah, a foolish youth shedding blood severely, while Abdullah ibn Mughaffal al-Muzani, Companion and one of seven sent by Umar to teach Basra, entered upon him saying, desist from what I see you do, for worst shepherds are the crushing. He said, what are you but refuse of Muhammad's Companions. He said, was there refuse among them, rather houses of honour. I bear I heard the Messenger say. > **""No imam or governor spending a dark night betraying his subjects but Allah forbids him Paradise.""** Then he left to the mosque and they saw his face. He was asked why speak to this fool publicly, and he said he had hidden knowledge he wished not to die till proclaiming. Then he told of being with the Messenger under a tree holding a branch lest it harm him, when he said, were dogs not a nation I hate to exterminate I would order killing them, so kill every jet black for it is a devil. Pray not in camel resting places for created of jinn, see their form and eyes, and pray in sheep pens for nearer mercy. The shaykh rose and soon sickened unto death, and Ubaydullah visited asking a covenant to act as he loves, asking will you act, he said yes. Part in Sahih on dogs."
"9073","In a version, he heard the Prophet say. > **""No imam spending night betraying his subjects but Allah forbids him Paradise whose fragrance is found on Resurrection from seventy years' journey.""**"
"9074","Anas ibn Malik, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that the Messenger said. > **""Whoever rules anything of the Muslims then betrays them is in Fire.""**"
"9075","Maqil ibn Yasar, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that the Messenger said. > **""Whoever rules any nation of my nation, few or many, and is not just among them, Allah shall hurl him on his face in Fire.""**"
"9076","In al-Saghir version, if he is not sincere to them nor strives for them as for himself. > **""If he is not sincere to them nor strives for them as his sincerity and striving for himself.""**"
"9077","Abu Bakrah and Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with them both, report that Umar sent Sad ibn Abi Waqqas as ruler of Kufa ordering him to sit for them and not veil. News reached Umar that he veiled and closed the door, so he sent Ammar ibn Yasir ordering if the door is closed to burn it, whether morning or evening. Ammar came to Kufa, burned his door and removed him."
"9078","Qays ibn Abi Hazim reports that Bilal came to Umar ibn al-Khattab in Sham surrounded by commanders and said, O Umar. He answered, here is Umar. Bilal said, you are between Allah and these, none between you and Allah. Look right, left, before, behind. These around you eat but bird meat. He said, true, by Allah I shall not rise till you guarantee each Muslim his food and share of oil and vinegar. They said, this is yours O Amir al-Muminin, Allah has widened provision for you."
"9079","Abu Musa, may Allah be pleased with him, said, the Commander of the Believers sent me to teach you your Lord's Book and your Prophet's practice and clear your roads."
"9080","Muhammad ibn Suqah reports that he came to Nuaym ibn Abi Hind who produced a document from Abu Ubaydah ibn al-Jarrah and Muadh ibn Jabal to Umar ibn al-Khattab, peace upon you, we knew you with self-concern, now you rule red and black of the nation, low and noble, foe and friend sit before you, each a share of justice, so consider yourself O Umar. We warn you a day faces humble, proofs severed before a conquering King's proof, creation submissive hoping mercy fearing punishment. We talked the nation's affair at latter times shall become open brothers secret foes, and we seek refuge that our letter lodge other than its heart place, written but as counsel. Umar wrote back, from Umar to Abu Ubaydah and Muadh, peace, your letter came reminding me of self-concern and my rule of this nation red and black. No might nor power for Umar therein but by Allah. You warn what nations before were warned, though night and day with people's terms near every far, bring every new and promised till people reach homes of Paradise and Fire. You warn the affair shall return to open brothers secret foes, but you are not they nor this its time, a time of desire and fear for worldly gain. You wrote seeking refuge I lodge your letter but where its heart, and you wrote as counsel, you spoke truth, so cease not writing me for I need you."
"9081","Abu Inabah, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that the Prophet said. > **""Burden not my nation. O Allah, whoever burdens my nation, take vengeance from him.""**"
"9082","Al-Miqdad ibn al-Aswad and Abu Umamah, may Allah be pleased with them both, report that the Messenger said. > **""When the ruler seeks suspicion among people he corrupts them.""** Abu Umamah's narration is in Abu Dawud."
"9083","Utbah ibn Abd and Abu Umamah, may Allah be pleased with them both, report that the Messenger said. > **""When the ruler seeks suspicion among people he corrupts them.""**"
"9084","Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, reports that the Prophet said, no one takes office but safety is spread for him. If he accepts it is spread and completed, if he shuns it what he cannot bear is opened. He was asked what shunning is, he said seeking slips and faults. > **""No one takes office but safety is spread for him. If he accepts it is spread and completed, and if he shuns it what he cannot bear is opened.""**"
"9085","Abu Bakrah, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that he heard the Messenger say. > **""Whoever honours Allah's sultan in this world, Allah honours him on Resurrection. Whoever degrades Allah's sultan in this world, Allah degrades him on Resurrection.""** Al-Tirmidhi reports only the degrading part. Al-Tabarani adds at start, the imam is Allah's shade on earth."
"9086","Jabir ibn Abdillah, may Allah be pleased with them both, reports that the Messenger said. > **""Of honouring Allah's majesty is honouring the grey Muslim, the just imam, and the Quran bearer who neither exaggerates therein nor shuns it.""**"
"9087","Abu Said al-Khudri, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that the Messenger addressed them saying in his sermon. > **""I am soon called and shall answer. Workers after me shall rule you doing what you do and what you know, and obedience to them is obedience.""** The full narration is in unjust rulers."
"9088","Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, reports that the Messenger said. > **""I have a right over you, and rulers have a right over you, as long as three stand: when mercy is sought they show mercy, when they judge they are just, when they covenant they fulfill. Whoever of them does not, upon him is curse of Allah, angels and all people. None of their obligatory or voluntary accepted.""**"
"9089","Hudhayfah, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that the Prophet said. > **""No folk marching to Allah's sultan to humiliate him but Allah humiliates them before Resurrection.""** Many narrations on hearing and obeying shall come."
"9090","Ubadah ibn al-Samit, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that the Prophet said, whoever worships Allah associating none, establishes prayer, gives zakah, hears and obeys, Allah admits him by whichever of Paradise's eight gates He wills. Whoever worships, prays, gives zakah, but hears and disobeys, Allah has choice, if He wills He mercies him and if He wills He punishes. > **""Whoever worships Allah associating none, establishes prayer, gives zakah, hears and obeys, Allah admits him by whichever of Paradise's eight gates He wills. Whoever hears and disobeys, Allah has choice, if He wills He mercies him and if He wills He punishes him.""**"
"9091","A man reports that they carried goods for Abu Dharr intending to give, sought him at al-Rabadhah finding he sought Hajj permission, and met him at Mina. It was said Uthman prayed four, and it weighed heavily and he spoke harshly saying, I prayed with the Messenger two, with Abu Bakr and Umar two. Then Abu Dharr rose and prayed four. He was asked, you faulted Amir al-Muminin then did it. He said, dissension is worse. The Messenger addressed them saying there shall be a sultan after me, humiliate him not. Whoever seeks to humiliate him casts Islam's yoke from his neck, his repentance unaccepted till he mends its breach, which he shall not, then returns among its strengtheners. The Messenger ordered them not to be overcome in three: commanding good, forbidding evil, teaching people the practices. > **""There shall be a sultan after me, so humiliate him not. Whoever seeks to humiliate him casts Islam's yoke from his neck. I command you not to be overcome in commanding good, forbidding evil and teaching the practices.""**"
"9092","Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, reports that the Messenger said. > **""Whoever works for Allah in unity and is right, Allah accepts from him, and if mistaken He forgives. Whoever works seeking division and is right, Allah accepts not, and if mistaken let him take his seat in Fire.""**"
"9093","Muawiyah, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that the Prophet said. > **""The hearing obedient has no proof against him, and the hearing disobedient has no proof for him.""** Abdullah said his father marked this addition doubting its reading."
"9094","Abu Sallam Mamtur reports from a Companion, likely Abu Malik al-Ashari, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger said. > **""I command you five: hearing and obedience, unity, migration and jihad in Allah's path. Whoever leaves unity a span casts Islam's yoke from his head. Whoever calls a call of ignorance is of Hell's throng.""** They said, O Messenger, though he fasts and prays. He said, though he fasts and prays, but name yourselves by Allah's name who named you His servants, Muslims, believers. Al-Tabarani adds, whoever parts unity a bow's span, no prayer nor fasting accepted, they are fuel of Fire."
"9095","Umar ibn Malik, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that the Messenger said. > **""I command you three and forbid you three: command you to associate none with Allah, hold to obedience altogether till Allah's order comes while upon it, and counsel your rulers who command you by Allah's order. Forbid you hearsay, much questioning and wasting wealth.""**"
"9096","A man reports that he reached the Prophet while he said. > **""O people, upon you is unity, and beware division.""** Thrice."
"9097","Al-Numan ibn Bashir, may Allah be pleased with them both, reports that the Messenger said upon these sticks or this minbar. > **""Whoever thanks not little thanks not much. Whoever thanks not people thanks not Allah. Speaking of Allah's blessing is thanks, leaving it ingratitude. Unity is mercy and division punishment.""** Abu Umamah al-Bahili said, upon you is the great multitude. Asked what it is, he recited the verse of al-Nur, if they turn, upon him is what he is charged and upon you what you are charged."
"9098","Abu Said al-Khudri, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that the Messenger said. > **""There shall be rulers over you whom hearts trust and skins soften to, then rulers over you from whom hearts recoil and skins shudder.""** A man asked, shall we fight them O Messenger. He said, no, as long as they establish prayer."
"9099","Abu Dharr, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that the Prophet said. > **""Two are better than one, three better than two, four better than three. Upon you is unity, for Allah shall not gather my nation but upon guidance.""**"
"9100","Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, reports that the Prophet said. > **""My nation shall never agree upon error. Upon you is unity, for Allah's Hand is upon unity.""**"
"9101","Usamah ibn Sharik, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that the Messenger said. > **""Allah's Hand is upon unity. When one strays, Satan snatches him as the wolf snatches the sheep from the flock.""**"
"9102","Muawiyah, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that the Messenger said. > **""Whoever dies without an imam dies an ignorant death.""**"
"9103","In a version, whoever dies without a pledge on his neck dies an ignorant death. > **""Whoever dies without a pledge on his neck dies an ignorant death.""**"
"9104","Abu Ishaq reports that he saw Hujr ibn Adi when Muawiyah seized him saying, this is my pledge I neither rescind nor seek rescission, in hearing of Allah and people."
"9105","Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that the Messenger said. > **""Rulers after me shall rule you, righteous by his righteousness and wicked by his wickedness. Hear and obey them in all accordant with truth. Pray behind them. If they do good, for you and them, and if evil, for you and upon them.""**"
"9106","Yus archaeological reports that when Uthman was killed Abu Masud secluded in his house, and he asked him of people's affair. He said, upon you is unity, for Allah did not gather Muhammad's nation upon error. Be patient till a righteous rests and rest from a wicked."
"9107","In a version from Yusayr, he met Abu Masud when Ali was killed and adjured him by Allah what he heard of tribulations. He said, we conceal nothing, upon you is piety and unity, beware division for it is error, for Allah would not gather Muhammad's nation upon error."
"9108","Muadh ibn Jabal, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that the Prophet of Allah said. > **""Satan is man's wolf as the wolf of sheep taking the far and edge sheep. Beware ravines, and upon you is unity, the multitude and the mosque.""**"
"9109","Muadh ibn Jabal, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that the Messenger said. > **""Paradise is not lawful for a disobedient. Whoever meets Allah breaking his pledge meets Him leprous. Whoever leaves unity a span deliberately casts Islam's yoke from his neck. Whoever dies with no obedience to an imam of unity dies an ignorant death.""**"
"9110","Abu al-Darda, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that the Messenger stood among them saying. > **""Paradise is not lawful for a disobedient. Whoever meets Allah breaking his pledge meets Him on Resurrection leprous. Whoever leaves obedience a span casts Islam's yoke from his neck. Whoever mornings with no obedience to a ruler of unity, Allah raises him as one dying an ignorant death, with a banner of treachery at his back on Resurrection.""**"
"9111","Bishr ibn Harb reports that Ibn Umar came to Abu Said asking, was I not told you pledged two rulers before people agreed on one. He said yes, I pledged Ibn al-Zubayr, then Syrians drove me to Hubaysh ibn Duljah and I pledged him. Ibn Umar said, this I feared, this I feared, and Hammad raised his voice. Abu Said said, O Abu Abd al-Rahman, did you not hear the Messenger say, whoever can not sleep a day nor morning nor evening but with a ruler over him. He said yes, but I dislike pledging two rulers before people agree on one. > **""Whoever can not sleep a day nor morning nor evening but with a ruler over him.""**"
"9112","Al-Miqdam ibn Madikarib, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that the Messenger said. > **""Obey your rulers whatever they are. If they command you of what I brought you they are rewarded and you rewarded by obeying. If they command you of what I brought not, it is upon them and you are free. For when you meet Allah you shall say, our Lord no injustice, and they shall say no injustice. You shall say, our Lord You sent messengers and we obeyed by Your permission, appointed successors and we obeyed by Your permission, appointed rulers and we obeyed by Your permission. He shall say, you spoke truth, it is upon them and you are free thereof.""**"
"9113","Al-Miqdam ibn Madikarib and Abu Umamah al-Bahili, may Allah be pleased with them both, report that a man came to the Messenger saying, if this affair is in your people enjoin them regarding us. He said, I remind you of Allah concerning my nation, transgress not upon my nation after me. Then he said to people, there shall be rulers after me, so render them obedience, for the ruler is like a shield shielded with. If they set your affairs right with good, for you and them. If they do evil in what they command, it is upon them and you are free. > **""I remind you of Allah concerning my nation, transgress not upon my nation after me. There shall be rulers after me, so render them obedience, for the ruler is like a shield shielded with. If they do evil it is upon them and you are free.""**"
"9114","Yazid ibn Salamah al-Jufi, may Allah be pleased with him, asked, O Messenger, if rulers after you take from us the right upon us and withhold the right Allah made for us, shall we fight and disobey them. The Prophet said, upon them is what they bear and upon you is what you bear. > **""Upon them is what they bear and upon you is what you bear.""**"
"9115","Abu Layla al-Ashari, Companion of the Messenger, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that the Messenger said, hold to obedience of your leaders and oppose them not, for their obedience is Allah's obedience and their disobedience Allah's disobedience. Allah sent me calling to His path with wisdom and good exhortation, so who succeeds me therein is my ally, and whoever rules you acting otherwise, upon him is curse of Allah, angels and all people. Rulers shall come who when mercy sought show none, when right asked give none, when good commanded deny, and you shall fear them and your assembly split till they burden you willingly or unwillingly, so least truth is take no stipend from them nor attend their assembly. > **""Hold to obedience of your leaders and oppose them not, for their obedience is Allah's obedience and their disobedience Allah's disobedience. Rulers shall come who when mercy sought show none, when right asked give none. Least truth is take no stipend from them nor attend their assembly.""**"
"9116","Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, reports that he saw the Messenger gesturing with his palm as measuring saying. > **""Whoever parts the Muslim unity a span, Islam's yoke leaves his neck. Opposers with their banners shall bear them on Resurrection behind their backs.""** Part in Sahih."
"9117","Sad ibn Junadah, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that the Messenger said, whoever parts unity is in Fire on his face. Allah says, who answers the distressed when he calls and removes evil and makes you successors on earth. So caliphate is from Allah, if good he takes it, if evil he is seized for it. Upon you is obedience in what Allah commanded. > **""Whoever parts unity is in Fire on his face. Caliphate is from Allah. Upon you is obedience in what Allah commanded.""**"
"9118","Fadalah ibn Ubayd, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that the Messenger said. > **""Three are not questioned: a man parting unity disobeying his imam dying disobedient, a slave fleeing his master, and a woman whose husband absent providing her worldly need then displaying adornment after him. They are not questioned.""**"
"9119","Al-Zibrqan ibn Badr, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that he came to the Messenger mentioning things, and al-Zibrqan said, we bear witness. He said, no, O Zibrqan, hear Allah and His Messenger and obey. He said, hearing and obedience to Allah and His Messenger. Thus found in the heard original. > **""O Zibrqan, hear Allah and His Messenger and obey.""**"
"9120","Amr al-Bikali, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that he heard the Messenger say. > **""When rulers over you command you prayer, zakah and jihad, reviling them is forbidden you and prayer behind them is lawful for you.""**"
"9121","In his version also, from Abu Tamimah who came to Sham seeking obligation and found a man circled by people, asking who, they said Amr al-Bikali whose hand was lost at Yarmuk when Romans left Sham, and he heard him say the Messenger said similar. > **""When rulers over you command you prayer, zakah and jihad, reviling them is forbidden you and prayer behind them is lawful for you.""**"
"9122","Adi ibn Hatim, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that they said, O Messenger, we ask not of obeying the pious reformer, but one doing such and such mentioning evil. He said. > **""Fear Allah and hear and obey.""**"
"9123","Arfajah, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that he heard the Messenger say. > **""Allah's Hand is with unity, and Satan with whoever opposes them rushing.""**"
"9124","Zirr ibn Hubaysh reports that when people denied al-Walid ibn Uqbah's conduct they fled to Abdullah ibn Masud, and Abdullah said, be patient, for fifty years of your imam's injustice is better than a month of chaos. For he heard the Messenger say, people must have rule righteous or wicked. The righteous judges justly in division and distributes your fay equally, the wicked tries the believer therein. And wicked rule is better than chaos. He was asked what is chaos, he said killing and lying. > **""People must have rule righteous or wicked. Wicked rule is better than chaos. Chaos is killing and lying.""**"
"9125","Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, reports that he was among companions when the Messenger came saying, do you not know I am Allah's Messenger to you. They said yes we bear you are Allah's Messenger. He said, do you not know whoever obeys me obeys Allah and of Allah's obedience is my obedience. They said yes we bear whoever obeys Allah obeys you and of Allah's obedience is your obedience. He said, of Allah's obedience is you obey me, and of my obedience is you obey your rulers. Obey your rulers, if they pray sitting pray sitting. > **""Do you not know I am Allah's Messenger to you. Of Allah's obedience is you obey me, and of my obedience is you obey your rulers. Obey your rulers, if they pray sitting pray sitting.""** Ahmad reports similar with imams instead of rulers."
"9126","Abdullah ibn Masud, may Allah be pleased with him, said, O people, upon you is obedience and unity for it is Allah's rope He commanded. What you dislike in unity is better than what you love in division. Long narration shall come in Tribulations."
"9127","Al-Harith ibn Qays reports that Abdullah ibn Masud said, O Harith ibn Qays, would you love to dwell mid Paradise. He said yes. He said, cling to the people's unity."
"9128","Ribi ibn Khirash reports that he went to Hudhayfah at al-Madain on nights people marched to Uthman, and he asked, O Ribi, what did your folk do. He asked which, he said those who went out to this man. He named some, and he said he heard the Messenger say. > **""Whoever parts unity and humiliates rule meets Allah with no face with Him.""**"
"9129","Asma bint Yazid, may Allah be pleased with her, reports that Abu Dharr served the Messenger and when done sheltered in the mosque sleeping therein as his home. The Messenger entered one night finding him sprawled, nudged him with his foot till he sat, asking do I see you sleeping. He said, O Messenger, where shall I sleep, have I another house. He sat with him asking, how when they expel you from it. He said, I join Sham for land of migration, gathering and prophets. He asked, how when expelled from Sham. He said, I return here as home. He asked, how when expelled a second time. He said, I take my sword fighting for myself till I die. He smiled fixing him with his hand saying, shall I guide to better than that. He said yes, may father and mother be for you. He said. > **""I see you sleeping. How when they expel you from it. Shall I guide to better than that. Submit to them where they lead you, and be driven where they drive you till you meet me upon that.""**"
"9130","Abu Dharr, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that the Prophet recited the verse, whoever fears Allah He makes him a way out and provides whence he reckons not, and whoever trusts Allah He suffices him, repeating till he drowsed, then said, O Abu Dharr, what when expelled from Madinah. He said, to ease I go as a dove of the Sanctuary. He said, what when expelled from Makkah. He said, to ease to Sham and the holy land. He said, what when expelled from Sham. He said, by Him who sent you with truth I place my sword on my shoulder. The Prophet said, better than that is hear and obey though an Abyssinian slave. Part of its end in Sahih and its start in Ibn Majah. > **""Whoever fears Allah He makes him a way out and provides whence he reckons not. Better than that is hear and obey though an Abyssinian slave.""**"
"9131","Amir ibn Rabiah, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that the Messenger said, whoever dies with no obedience upon him dies an ignorant death. If he casts it after عقدing it on his neck he meets Allah with no proof. Let no man seclude with a woman, for their third is Satan, except a mahram. Satan is with one and farther from two. Whose evil displeases him and good pleases him is a believer. > **""Whoever dies with no obedience upon him dies an ignorant death. If he casts it after عقدing it on his neck he meets Allah with no proof. Let no man seclude with a woman, for their third is Satan. Whose evil displeases him and good pleases him is a believer.""**"
"9132","Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said prayer to the prayer before it is expiation except for three, and they knew a new matter came. Except associating with Allah, breaking the bargain, and abandoning the Sunnah. As for breaking the bargain, it is to give a man your pledge then fight him with your sword. As for leaving the Sunnah, it is leaving the unity. > **""Prayer to the prayer before it is expiation except for three. Except associating with Allah, breaking the bargain, and abandoning the Sunnah. Breaking the bargain is to give a man your pledge then fight him with your sword. Leaving the Sunnah is leaving the unity.""**"
"9133","Uqbah ibn Amir, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that the Messenger of Allah said, shall I tell you of the best of your workers and the worst. They said yes O Messenger. He said, their best for you are those you love and who love you, you supplicate for them and they supplicate for you. Their worst for you are those you hate and who hate you, you supplicate against them and they supplicate against you. They asked, shall we fight them. He said, no, leave them as long as they fast and pray. > **""Shall I tell you of the best of your workers and the worst. Their best are those you love and who love you. Their worst are those you hate and who hate you. No, leave them as long as they fast and pray.""**"
"9134","Zayd ibn Wahb reports that people objected to a ruler in Hudhayfah's time, and a man came through the great mosque till he stood over Hudhayfah sitting in a circle and said, O Companion of the Messenger, will you not command good and forbid evil. Hudhayfah raised his head perceiving his intent and said, commanding good and forbidding evil is good, but it is not of the Sunnah to brandish a weapon against your ruler."
"9135","Jabalah, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that the Messenger of Allah said. > **""Whoever parts unity a span has parted Islam.""**"
"9136","Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, reports that the Messenger of Allah said. > **""Whoever parts unity a span or a bowspan casts Islam's yoke from his neck. Whoever dies with no imam over him, his death is an ignorant death. Whoever dies under a banner of partisanship calling to or aiding partisanship, his killing is an ignorant killing.""**"
"9137","Abdullah ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, reports that he heard the Messenger of Allah say. > **""Whoever gives a pledge then breaks it meets Allah with no oath with him.""**"
"9138","Muawiyah ibn Abi Sufyan, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that the Messenger of Allah said. > **""Whoever dies with no imam over him dies an ignorant death.""**"
"9139","Al-Ashtar reports that Umar ibn al-Khattab mentioned the Messenger said to them. > **""Allah's Hand is with unity and the lone is with Satan. Truth is a root in Paradise and falsehood a root in Fire.""**"
"9140","Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, reports that the Messenger said, preserve me in my Companions, then those after them, then those after them. Then lying shall appear till a man testifies before he is asked and swears before he is asked and spends himself for false speech. Whoever delights in the midst of Paradise, let him cling to unity, for Allah's Hand is upon unity. Satan is with one and farther from two. Let no man seclude with a woman, for their third is Satan. Whose evil displeases him and good pleases him is a believer. > **""Preserve me in my Companions, then those after them, then those after them. Then lying shall appear. Whoever delights in the midst of Paradise, let him cling to unity, for Allah's Hand is upon unity. Satan is with one and farther from two. Let no man seclude with a woman, for their third is Satan. Whose evil displeases him and good pleases him is a believer.""**"
"9141","Anas ibn Malik, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that Muadh ibn Jabal asked, O Messenger, if rulers over us follow not your practice nor take your order, what do you command. The Messenger said. > **""No obedience to one who obeys not Allah.""**"
"9142","Abdullah ibn al-Samit reports that Ziyad wished to send Imran ibn Husayn over Khurasan and he refused. His companions asked, did you leave Khurasan. He said, by Allah I delight not to burn with its heat while they cool, fearing in the enemy's throat a letter from Ziyad comes, if I proceed I perish and if I return my neck is struck. Then he sought al-Hakam ibn Amr al-Ghifari who accepted. Imran asked for al-Hakam to be called, and when he came Imran asked, did you hear the Messenger say there is no obedience to anyone in disobedience of Allah. He said yes. Imran said, praise be to Allah, or Allah is Greatest. > **""No obedience to anyone in disobedience of Allah.""**"
"9143","In a version from al-Hasan, Ziyad employed al-Hakam al-Ghifari over an army and Imran ibn Husayn met him among people asking, do you know why I came. He asked why. He said, do you recall the Messenger's word to the man whose commander said fall in fire but he was caught and held back, and when told the Messenger said had he fallen both would enter Fire, no obedience in disobedience of Allah. He said yes. He said, I only wished to remind you of this narration. In some paths, no obedience to a creature in disobedience of the Creator. > **""Had he fallen therein both would enter Fire. No obedience in disobedience of Allah. No obedience to a creature in disobedience of the Creator.""**"
"9144","Imran and al-Hakam ibn Amr al-Ghifari, may Allah be pleased with them both, report that the Messenger of Allah said. > **""No obedience in disobedience of Allah.""**"
"9145","Ismail ibn Ubayd al-Ansari reports the narration in which Ubadah, may Allah have mercy on him, said to Abu Hurayrah, you were not with us when we pledged the Messenger to hear and obey in energy and laziness, spend in hardship and ease, command good forbid evil, speak for Allah fearing no blame, and aid the Prophet when he comes to Yathrib protecting him as ourselves sons and wives, and ours is Paradise. This is the pledge, who breaks harms himself, who fulfills Allah fulfills for him. Then Muawiyah wrote to Uthman that Ubadah corrupted Sham and its folk, either restrain him or leave him to Sham. Uthman wrote, mount Ubadah back to his home in Madinah. Ubadah came to Uthman in the house with only a predecessor present, and Uthman turned saying, O Ubadah what is ours and yours. Ubadah stood among people saying, I heard the Messenger Abul Qasim Muhammad say, rulers after me shall rule you enjoining what you deny and denying what you know, so no obedience to who disobeys Allah, make no excuse by your Lord. > **""We pledged him to hear and obey in energy and laziness, spend in hardship and ease, command good forbid evil, speak for Allah fearing no blame. Rulers after me shall enjoin what you deny and deny what you know, so no obedience to who disobeys Allah.""**"
"9146","Bilal ibn Buqtr reports that a Companion of the Prophet was employed over Sijistan, and another Companion met him saying, do you recall when the Messenger employed a man over an army with a kindled fire and he told a companion rise and enter it, and when it reached the Messenger he said had he entered both would enter Fire, no obedience in disobedience of Allah. I only wished to remind you this. > **""Had he entered therein both would enter Fire. No obedience in disobedience of Allah.""**"
"9147","In a version, rise and enter it, but he refused and he insisted. > **""Rise and enter it.""**"
"9148","In a version, no obedience in disobedience of Allah, and he said yes. > **""No obedience in disobedience of Allah.""**"
"9149","Ubadah ibn al-Samit, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that while in Sham donkeys bearing wine passed him, so he took a blade from the market and tore them, then said, we pledged the Messenger to hear and obey in energy and laziness, hardship and ease, command good forbid evil, speak for Allah fearing no blame, and aid the wronged protecting him as ourselves and sons. Then he mentioned the narration. > **""We pledged the Messenger to hear and obey in energy and laziness, hardship and ease, command good forbid evil, speak for Allah fearing no blame of a blamer.""**"
"9150","Sad ibn Ubadah, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that the Prophet said. > **""O Sad, upon you is hearing and obedience in hardship and ease, energy and dislike. Dispute not the affair with its folk unless they call you to خلاف what is in Allah's Book. If they call you to خلاف what is in Allah's Book, follow Allah's Book.""**"
"9151","Abu Utbah al-Khawlani, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that the Messenger of Allah said. > **""Burden not my nation, burden not my nation, burden not my nation. O Allah, whoever commands my nation what You commanded them not, they are free of him.""**"
"9152","Ubadah ibn al-Samit, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that the Messenger of Allah said. > **""There shall be rulers after me commanding you what you know and doing what you deny, and those are no imams over you.""**"
"9153","Muadh ibn Jabal, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that he heard the Messenger say, take the stipend while it is a gift. When it becomes a bribe for religion take it not, yet you shall not leave it, poverty and need preventing you. Verily the mill of Islam turns, so turn with the Book where it turns. The Book and the sultan shall part, so part not the Book. Rulers over you shall judge for themselves what they judge not for you. If you disobey they kill you, if you obey they misguide you. They asked, O Messenger, what to do. He said, as the companions of Isa son of Maryam did, sawn with saws and carried upon wood. Death in obedience of Allah is better than life in His disobedience. > **""Take the stipend while it is a gift. When it becomes a bribe for religion take it not. Turn with the Book where it turns. Part not the Book. Death in obedience of Allah is better than life in disobedience of Allah.""**"
"9154","Abu Sulalah, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that the Prophet said. > **""There shall be leaders over you owning your provisions, speaking to you lying, acting doing evil. They are not pleased with you till you beautify their ugly and affirm their lie. Give them the right while they are pleased with it. When they exceed, whoever is killed thereupon is a martyr.""**"
"9155","Abu Hisham al-Sulami, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that the Messenger said. > **""There shall be leaders over you owning your necks, speaking to you lying, acting doing evil. They are not pleased till you beautify their ugly and affirm their lie. Give them the right while they are pleased with it.""**"
"9156","Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, reports that the Messenger said. > **""There shall be rulers after me knowing and denying. Whoever opposes them is saved, whoever isolates from them is safe, whoever mixes with them is destroyed.""**"
"9157","Thawban, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that the Messenger of Allah said. > **""Be upright to Quraysh while they are upright to you. When they are not, place your swords on your shoulders and annihilate their green. If you do not, be then wretched farmers eating from toil of your hands.""**"
"9158","Al-Numan ibn Bashir, may Allah be pleased with them both, reports that he heard the Messenger say. > **""Be upright to Quraysh while they are upright to you. If they are not upright to you, place your swords on your shoulders and annihilate their green.""**"
"9159","Muadh ibn Jabal, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that the Messenger said, the most I fear for my nation are three: a man reading Allah's Book till its splendour appears upon him with Islam's cloak Allah lent him, then unsheathes his sword striking his neighbour accusing him of idolatry. Asked, O Messenger, accuser or accused worthier, he said the accuser. A man given rule saying, who obeys me obeys Allah and who disobeys me disobeys Allah, lying, for no caliph may be a shield دون the Creator. A man trifling with narrations, whenever one ends telling longer, till he reaches the Dajjal following him. > **""The most I fear for my nation are three. A man reading Allah's Book then striking his neighbour accusing him of idolatry. A man given rule claiming obedience to him is obedience to Allah. A man trifling with narrations till he reaches the Dajjal following him.""**"
"9160","Maghra reports that when Ibn Amir came to Sham, whomever Allah willed of the Prophet's Companions and others came to him except Abu al-Darda. He said, Abu al-Darda came not to me, I shall go to him fulfilling his right. He came greeting saying, your companions came but you came not, so I wished to come fulfilling your right. Abu al-Darda said, never were you smaller in Allah's eye nor mine than today. The Messenger ordered us to change for you when you change."
"9161","Shurayh ibn Ubayd and others report that Iyad ibn Ghanm flogged a house owner when it was opened, and Hisham ibn Hakim rebuked him harshly till Iyad angered. After nights Hisham came apologizing, then said, did you not hear the Messenger say the severest torment are those most tormenting people in this world. Iyad ibn Ghanm said, O Hisham we heard what you heard and saw what you saw. Did you not hear the Messenger say, whoever wishes to counsel a sultan in a matter, let him not show openly, but take his hand in privacy. If he accepts then so, else he discharged his duty. And you O Hisham are bold, daring against Allah's sultan. Did you not fear the sultan kills you becoming slain of Allah's sultan. Part in Sahih from Hisham alone. > **""The severest torment are those most tormenting people in this world. Whoever wishes to counsel a sultan, let him not show openly, but take his hand in privacy. If he accepts then so, else he discharged his duty.""**"
"9162","Jubayr ibn Nufayr reports that Iyad ibn Ghanm punished a house owner when opened, and Hisham ibn Hakim rebuked him harshly. After nights Hisham came apologizing saying, O Iyad, know you not the Messenger said the severest torment on Resurrection are those most tormenting people in this world. Iyad said, we heard what you heard, saw what you saw, companied whom you companied. Did you not hear O Hisham the Messenger say, whoever has counsel, then he mentioned similar. Its men trustworthy, chain connected. > **""The severest torment on the Day of Resurrection are those most tormenting people in this world. Whoever has counsel for a sultan, let him take his hand in privacy.""**"
"9163","Said ibn Jumhan reports that he met Abdullah ibn Abi Awfa blind in sight and greeted. He asked who, he said Said ibn Jumhan. He asked of his father, he said the Azariqah killed him. He said, may Allah curse the Azariqah. The Messenger told us they are dogs of Fire. He asked, Azariqah alone or all Khawarij, he said all Khawarij. He asked, the sultan wrongs people doing this and that. He took his hand squeezing hard saying, woe to you O Ibn Jumhan, upon you is the greatest multitude, twice. If the sultan hears from you, come to his house informing what you know. If he accepts then so, else leave him, for you know not more than he. Part in Ibn Majah."
"9164","Abdullah ibn Masud, may Allah be pleased with him, said, rulers over you shall leave of the Sunnah like this. If you leave it they make it like this. If you leave it they bring the great calamity."
"9165","Umar al-Laythi reports that a question grieved him he asked not the Messenger nor heard asked, so he awaited. One day he entered while he performed ablution, finding him free and pleasant, two states he loved. He asked permission to ask, and he said ask what occurs. He asked, what is faith, he said patience and tolerance. Who has best faith, best character. Who has best Islam, from whose hand and tongue people are safe. What jihad is best. He lowered his head silent long till he feared burdening him, recalling yesterday he said the greatest crime among Muslims is asking of what was not forbidden then forbidden for his asking. He sought refuge from Allah's and His Messenger's anger. He raised his head asking how he said. He said, what jihad is best. He said, a word of justice before an unjust imam. Similar narrations shall come in denouncing evil. > **""Faith is patience and tolerance. The best in faith are best in character. The best in Islam are those from whose hand and tongue people are safe. The best jihad is a word of justice before an unjust imam.""**"
"9166","Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that the Messenger of Allah said. > **""O Abu Hurayrah, enter not upon rulers. If you are overcome thereby, exceed not my practice. Fear not their sword and whip to command them to fear Allah.""**"
"9167","Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, reports that the Messenger of Allah said. > **""Whoever attends a ruler, let him speak good or be silent.""**"
"9168","Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that charity camels passed the Messenger and he reached to a wool from a camel's side saying. > **""I have no more right to this wool than any Muslim man.""**"
"9169","Abdullah ibn Zurayr reports that he entered upon Ali ibn Abi Talib, Hasan said on the day of sacrifice, and he brought khazirah. He said, may Allah set you right, would you bring of this duck, meaning geese, for Allah increased good. He said, O Ibn Zurayr, I heard the Messenger say. > **""Nothing is lawful for a caliph of Allah's wealth but two bowls: a bowl he and his family eat, and a bowl he places before people.""**"
"9170","Al-Hasan ibn Ali, may Allah be pleased with them both, reports that when Abu Bakr was dying he said, O Aishah, look to the milch camel whose milk we drank, the bowl we ate in, the velvet we wore. We benefited thereby while ruling Muslims. When I die return it to Umar. When Abu Bakr died she sent it to Umar, and Umar said, may Allah have mercy on you, you tired whoever comes after you."
"9171","Sad ibn Tamim, a Companion, reports that he asked, O Messenger, what is for the caliph after you. He said. > **""What is for me, while he shows mercy to kin, is equitable in equity and just in division.""**"
"9172","Amr ibn Abi Aqrab reports that he heard Attab ibn Usayd, leaning his back to the House of Allah, say, by Allah I gained in this office the Messenger gave me but two knotted garments which I clothed my freedman Kaysan with."
"9173","Amr ibn al-As, may Allah be pleased with him, said, if Abu Bakr and Umar left this wealth we were cheated and their opinion strayed. By Allah, they were neither cheated nor deficient in opinion. If it was not lawful for them and we take it after them we perish. By Allah, delusion comes but from us."
"9174","Qays ibn Sad ibn Ubadah reports that the Messenger of Allah said. > **""Whoever strengthens his sultan by disobedience of Allah, Allah weakens his plot till the Day of Resurrection.""**"
"9175","Yazid ibn Abi Sufyan reports that Abu Bakr, may Allah have mercy on him, said when sending him to Sham, O Yazid you have kin and may favour them with office, my greatest fear for you. The Messenger said, whoever rules anything of the Muslims then appoints over them one by favouritism, upon him is Allah's curse. Allah accepts from him neither صرف nor عدل till He admits him to Hell. Whoever grants Allah's preserve then violates it without right, upon him is Allah's curse, or Allah's covenant is free of him. > **""Whoever rules anything of the Muslims then appoints over them one by favouritism, upon him is Allah's curse. Allah accepts from him neither صرف nor عدل till He admits him to Hell.""**"
"9176","Hudhayfah, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that the Messenger struck for them parables one three five seven nine eleven. He struck one leaving the rest saying, a folk weak and poor fought by tyrannical hostile folk, and Allah made the weak prevail. Then they turned to their enemy employing and empowering them, angering Allah upon them till the day they meet Him. > **""A folk weak and poor fought by tyrannical hostile folk, and Allah made the weak prevail. Then they employed their enemy empowering them, angering Allah upon them till the day they meet Him.""**"
"9177","Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that the Messenger of Allah said. > **""In the end of time are unjust rulers, sinful ministers, treacherous judges and lying scholars. Whoever of you reaches that time, let him not be their collector, overseer nor policeman.""**"
"9178","Abu al-Walid al-Qurashi reports that he was with Bilal ibn Abi Burdah when a man of Abd al-Qays came saying, may Allah set the ruler right, people of al-Taff pay not zakah of their wealth. He knew what he said and told the ruler, who asked his tribe and name, such son of such. He wrote to his police chief, send to Abd al-Qays asking of such son of such, how is his lineage among them. The messenger returned finding his lineage impugned. He said, Allah is Greatest. My father told me from my grandfather Abu Musa that the Messenger said, none rebels against people but a base-born child or one with its vein. Abu al-Walid said, strives. The rest trustworthy, Abu al-Walid unknown. > **""None rebels against people but a base-born child or one with its vein therein.""**"
"9179","Masud ibn Qabisah or Qabisah ibn Masud reports that this clan of Muharib prayed Fajr, and when they prayed a youth among them said, I heard the Messenger say. > **""The easts of the earth and its wests shall be opened for you. Their workers are in Fire except who fears Allah and renders trust.""**"
"9180","Muadh ibn Jabal, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that the Messenger of Allah said. > **""The Hour shall not rise till Allah sends lying rulers, wicked ministers, treacherous trustees and sinful reciters, their mark monks with no desire, or flock, or moisture. Allah clothes them a dusty dark trial wherein they plunge as Jews plunge in injustice.""**"
"9181","Abu Umamah, may Allah be pleased with him, mentions the Messenger said. > **""In this nation at the end of time, or men of this nation shall emerge at the end of time with whips as cow tails, morning in Allah's wrath and evening in His anger.""**"
"9182","In his version, beware to be of their entourage. Ahmad's men trustworthy. > **""Beware to be of their entourage.""**"
"9183","Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that he heard the Messenger say. > **""If your life prolongs you shall soon see folk morning in Allah's wrath and evening in Allah's curse, in their hands like cow tails.""**"
"9184","Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that they saw all the Messenger told them except he said men told on Resurrection, lay your whips and enter Fire. > **""Men told on the Day of Resurrection: lay your whips and enter Fire.""**"
"9185","Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that the Messenger said, can none of you recite in a night, Say He Allah is One, for it equals all Quran. He said, people must have an overseer and the overseer is in Fire. The policeman is brought on Resurrection told, lay your whip and enter Fire. > **""Can none of you recite in a night: Say He Allah is One, for it equals all Quran. People must have an overseer and the overseer is in Fire. Policeman brought on the Day of Resurrection is told: lay your whip and enter Fire.""**"
"9186","Al-Shabi reports that Abu Hurayrah saw a man admiring his appearance asking, of whom is the man. He said of those Allah blessed. He said, all of us blessed, of whom are you. He said of earth folk. He said, all of earth folk, of whom. He said of the Nabateans. He said, away from me. I heard the Messenger say, killers of prophets and helpers of oppressors. When they take lands and raise buildings, flee flee. > **""Killers of prophets and helpers of oppressors. When they take lands and raise buildings, flee flee.""**"
"9187","Khalid ibn Hakim ibn Hizam reports that Abu Ubaydah seized a man with something and Khalid ibn al-Walid forbade him saying, you angered the ruler. He came saying, I meant not to anger you, but I heard the Messenger say. > **""The severest torment on Resurrection are those most tormenting people in this world.""** Ahmad adds, go and free their way. Counsel of rulers preceded."
"9188","Muadh ibn Jabal, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that the Messenger said, beware injustice for injustice is darkness on Resurrection. Beware miserliness, for it destroyed those before you. It commanded severing kin so they severed, commanded shedding blood so they shed. A man stood asking, O Messenger, what Islam is best. The Messenger said, from whose hand and tongue people are safe. > **""Beware injustice for injustice is darkness on the Day of Resurrection. Beware miserliness, for it destroyed those before you. It commanded severing kin so they severed, commanded shedding blood so they shed. The best in Islam is one from whose hand and tongue people are safe.""**"
"9189","Al-Hirmas ibn Ziyad, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that he saw the Messenger preaching on his camel saying. > **""Beware treachery for it is an evil entourage. Beware injustice for it is darkness on Resurrection. Beware miserliness, for it destroyed those before you till they shed blood and severed kin.""**"
"9190","Al-Miswar ibn Makhramah, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that the Messenger said. > **""Beware injustice for injustice is darkness on the Day of Resurrection.""**"
"9191","Ibn Masud, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that the Prophet said. > **""Wrong not, lest you supplicate unanswered, seek rain unwatered, seek help unaided.""**"
"9192","Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, reports that the Prophet said. > **""Fear injustice for it is darkness on the Day of Resurrection.""**"
"9193","Urwah ibn Muhammad ibn Atiyyah reports from his father from his grandfather that the Messenger of Allah said. > **""When the sultan rages Satan prevails.""**"
"9194","Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, reports that the Messenger of Allah said. > **""Rulers over you worse than the Magians.""**"
"9195","Abu Umamah, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that the Messenger said. > **""Two kinds of my nation my intercession reaches not: an unjust treacherous imam and every extremist seceder.""**"
"9196","Maqil ibn Yasar, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that the Messenger of Allah said. > **""Two men of my nation my intercession reaches not: an unjust treacherous sultan, and another extremist in religion seceding from it.""**"
"9197","In a version, two kinds of my nation my intercession reaches not: an unjust treacherous sultan, and an extremist in religion testifying against them disavowing them. > **""Two kinds of my nation my intercession reaches not: an unjust treacherous sultan, and an extremist in religion testifying against them disavowing them.""**"
"9198","Ibn Masud, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that the Messenger said. > **""The severest torment of Fire folk on Resurrection are one killing a prophet or killed by a prophet, or an unjust imam.""** Part in Sahih. Al-Bazzar says an imam of misguidance."
"9199","Abu Qubayl reports that Muawiyah ibn Abi Sufyan ascended the minbar Friday saying in his sermon, wealth is ours and fay is ours. Whom we will we give, whom we will we withhold, and none answered. The second Friday likewise, none answered. The third Friday likewise, and a man attending the mosque stood saying, nay, wealth is ours and fay is ours. Whoever bars us therefrom we sue him to Allah with our swords. Muawiyah descended sending for the man admitting him. Folk said the man perished. Then people entered finding him with him upon the couch, and Muawiyah said to people, this revived me, may Allah revive him. I heard the Messenger say, rulers after me shall speak unanswered, plunging in Fire as monkeys plunge. I spoke first Friday unanswered fearing I am of them, second Friday saying in myself I am of the folk, third this man answered reviving me, may Allah revive him. > **""Rulers after me shall speak unanswered, plunging in Fire as monkeys plunge.""**"
"9200","Abu Said al-Khudri, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that the Messenger of Allah said. > **""The severest torment on Resurrection is an unjust imam.""**"
"9201","Abu Said, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that the Messenger addressed them saying in his sermon, I am soon called and shall answer. Workers after me shall rule you doing what you know and what you recognize, and obedience to them is obedience. You remain so a time, then workers after them rule you doing what you know not and what you recognize not. Whoever follows and counsels them is destroyed and destroys. Mingle bodies part deeds. Testify the good is good and the evil is evil. > **""I am soon called and shall answer. Workers after me shall rule you doing what you know and what you recognize, and obedience to them is obedience. Then workers after them rule you doing what you know not and what you recognize not. Mingle bodies part deeds. Testify the good is good and the evil is evil.""**"
"9202","Jabir ibn Samurah, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that he heard the Messenger say. > **""Three I fear for my nation: seeking cure by stars, injustice of the sultan, and denial of divine decree.""**"
"9203","Umar ibn Bilal reports that he saw Abdullah ibn Busr, Companion of the Messenger, old seated in the mosque, when his slave came saying, master your camels seized in forced labour of al-Rilah, meaning the house of al-Abbas ibn al-Walid at Hims mosque gate. With two men holding his arms he rose, and Umar walked with him to al-Rilah finding his camels kneeled and them sifting dust with sacks. He took a sack opening for them, and Christians said, this is your Prophet's Companion you do this, had we seen a companion of Isa we would carry him on heads. Folk moved to seize him, and he said, leave me. I heard the Messenger say, how are you when rulers oppress you. > **""How are you when rulers oppress you.""**"
"9204","Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that he heard the Messenger say. > **""O Allah, I seek refuge in You from haraj imams who drive my nation to injustice.""**"
"9205","Abdullah ibn Amr, may Allah be pleased with them both, reports that the Prophet said, three Allah looks not at on Resurrection nor purifies with painful torment: a man coming to a united Islam splitting their staff till they permit sacred and shed blood, and an unjust sultan saying, who obeys me obeys Allah and who disobeys me disobeys Allah. Sufyan was silent of the third mentioning it not. > **""Three Allah looks not at on the Day of Resurrection nor purifies with painful torment: a man coming to a united Islam splitting their staff till they permit sacred and shed blood, and an unjust sultan saying, who obeys me obeys Allah and who disobeys me disobeys Allah.""**"
"9206","Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that the Prophet said. > **""After me are leaders giving wisdom on their minbars. When they descend it is stripped from them. Their bodies are worse than carrion.""**"
"9207","Abu Barzah, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that he heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say. > **""After me are leaders. If you obey them they disbelieve you, if you disobey them they kill you. Imams of disbelief and heads of error.""**"
"9208","Muadh ibn Jabal, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that he heard the Messenger say, take the stipend while it is a gift. When it becomes a bribe for religion take it not, yet you shall not leave it, poverty and need preventing you. The mill of Bani Marah turned and Bani Marah were killed. Verily the mill of Islam turns, so turn with the Book where it turns. The Book and the sultan shall part, so part not the Book. Rulers over you shall judge for themselves what they judge not for you. If you disobey they kill you, if you obey they misguide you. They asked, O Messenger, what to do. He said, as the companions of Isa son of Maryam did, sawn with saws and carried upon wood. Death in obedience of Allah is better than life in His disobedience. > **""Take the stipend while it is a gift. When it becomes a bribe for religion take it not. Turn with the Book where it turns. Part not the Book. Death in obedience of Allah is better than life in disobedience of Allah.""**"
"9209","Ubadah ibn al-Samit, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that the Messenger mentioned rulers saying, rulers over you, if you obey them they enter you Fire, if you disobey they kill you. A man among them said, O Messenger, name them that we may throw dust in their faces. The Messenger said, perhaps they throw in your face and gouge your eye. > **""Rulers over you, if you obey them they enter you Fire, if you disobey they kill you.""**"
"9210","Kab ibn Ujrah, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that the Messenger came out to them saying, rulers after me preaching wisdom on minbars, when they descend it is snatched from them and their hearts are fouler than carrion. Then he mentioned the narration. > **""Rulers after me preaching wisdom on minbars, when they descend it is snatched from them and their hearts are fouler than carrion.""**"
"9211","Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, reports that the Messenger of Allah said. > **""A man of Qahtan shall surely drive people with his staff.""**"
"9212","Abu Dharr, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that he walked with the Messenger who said thrice, other than the Dajjal frightens me more for my nation. He asked, O Messenger, what other than the Dajjal frightens you for your nation. He said, misguiding leaders. > **""Other than the Dajjal frightens me more for my nation, thrice. Misguiding leaders.""**"
"9213","Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that they sat with the Prophet while he slept and mentioned the Dajjal. He awoke red-faced saying, other than the Dajjal, in my view more feared for my nation over you: misguiding leaders. > **""Other than the Dajjal, more feared for my nation over you: misguiding leaders.""**"
"9214","Umayr ibn Sad, whom Umar appointed over Hims, reports that Umar said to Kab, I ask you of a matter conceal it not. He said, by Allah I conceal nothing I know. He asked, what most do you fear for Muhammad's nation. He said, misguiding leaders. Umar said, you spoke truth, the Messenger confided that to me informing me."
"9215","Thawban, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that the Messenger of Allah said. > **""I fear for my nation only the misguiding leaders.""**"
"9216","Abu al-Darda, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that the Messenger covenanted to them. > **""The most I fear for my nation are the misguiding leaders.""**"
"9217","Shaddad ibn Aws, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that the Messenger of Allah said. > **""I fear for my nation only the misguiding leaders. When the sword is placed in my nation it is not lifted from them till the Day of Resurrection.""**"
"9218","Abu Umamah, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that he heard the Messenger say. > **""I fear not for my nation hunger killing them nor an enemy destroying them. I fear for my nation misguiding leaders. If they obey them they trial them, if they disobey they kill them.""**"
"9219","Abu al-Awar al-Sulami, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that he heard the Messenger say. > **""The most I fear for my nation are obeyed miserliness, followed desire and an erring imam.""**"
"9220","Amr ibn Awf, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that he heard the Messenger say, I fear for my nation after me three deeds. They asked what, O Messenger. He said, slip of the scholar, unjust rule and followed desire. > **""I fear for my nation after me three deeds. Slip of the scholar, unjust rule and followed desire.""**"
"9221","Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that the Messenger of Allah said. > **""The worst governors are the crushing.""**"
"9222","Hudhayfah, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that the Messenger of Allah said. > **""As if you with a rider coming to you alighting among you saying: the land is our land, the city our city, you are but our slaves and hirelings. Then barring widows, orphans and what Allah bestowed upon their imam.""**"
"9223","Mahdi reports that Ibn Masud said, how are you O Mahdi when your best are overcome, your youths and worst employed over you, and prayer prayed out of time. He said, I know not. He said, be not collector, overseer, policeman nor courier. Pray prayer at its time. Mahdi unknown, rest men of Sahih."
"9224","In a version from Ibrahim, Abdullah prayed it with them when they delayed little, seeing they bear its sin. Its men men of Sahih except Ibrahim did not meet Ibn Masud."
"9225","Abu Said and Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with them both, report that the Messenger said. > **""A time shall surely come over people with foolish rulers advancing the worst, overcoming the best, delaying prayer from its times. Whoever of you reaches it, let him not be overseer, policeman, collector nor treasurer.""**"
"9226","Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that a boy was born to the brother of Umm Salamah, wife of the Messenger, and they named him al-Walid. The Prophet said. > **""You named him by names of your pharaohs. There shall be in this nation a man called al-Walid, more evil to this nation than Pharaoh to his folk.""**"
"9227","Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that he heard the Messenger say, a tyrant of Umayyad tyrants shall surely nosebleed upon my minbar and his nosebleed flows. One who saw Amr ibn Said ibn al-As nosebleed upon the Messenger's minbar till it flowed told him. > **""A tyrant of Umayyad tyrants shall surely nosebleed upon my minbar and his nosebleed flows.""**"
"9228","Abu Yahya reports that he was between al-Hasan and al-Husayn while al-Husayn and Marwan reviled each other, and al-Hasan restrained al-Husayn. Marwan said, a cursed household. Al-Hasan angered saying, did you say a cursed household. By Allah, Allah cursed you upon His Prophet's tongue while in your father's loins."
"9229","In a version, al-Hasan and al-Husayn said, by Allah then by Allah, Allah cursed you, and the rest similar."
"9230","Al-Shabi reports that he heard Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr leaning on the Kabah saying, by this Kabah's Lord, the Messenger cursed so-and-so unborn from his loins. Ahmad and al-Bazzar report, except he said Allah cursed al-Hakam and his issue upon His Prophet's tongue. Al-Tabarani similar, and Ahmad's men men of Sahih."
"9231","Abu Said al-Khudri, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that the Messenger said. > **""When Bani Abi Fulan reach thirty men they take Allah's wealth as fortune, Allah's religion as intrusion, Allah's servants as servants.""** Ahmad and al-Bazzar say Bani Abi al-As. Al-Tabarani in al-Awsat and Abu Yala, with weakness, rest men of Sahih."
"9232","Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, said, when Bani Abi al-As reach thirty, Allah's religion is intrusion, Allah's wealth fortune, Allah's servants servants."
"9233","Abdullah ibn Amr, may Allah be pleased with them both, reports that they sat with the Prophet while Amr ibn al-As went to dress to join him, and he said while with him, a cursed man shall surely enter upon you. By Allah he remained anxious watching in and out till so-and-so entered, meaning al-Hakam. Ahmad and al-Bazzar say till al-Hakam ibn Abi al-As entered. Al-Tabarani in al-Awsat, Ahmad's men men of Sahih. > **""A cursed man shall surely enter upon you.""**"
"9234","Jubayr ibn Mutim, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that while sitting with the Prophet in al-Hijr, al-Hakam ibn Abi al-As passed and the Prophet said. > **""Woe to my nation from what is in this one's loins.""**"
"9235","Abdullah al-Bahi, freedman of al-Zubayr, reports that he was in the mosque while Marwan preached, and Abdur Rahman ibn Abi Bakr said, by Allah Abu Bakr appointed none of his folk successor. Marwan said, you are in whom was revealed, he who says to his parents fie. Abdur Rahman said, you lied, but the Messenger cursed your father."
"9236","Abu Ubaydah ibn al-Jarrah, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that the Messenger said. > **""This affair of my nation shall ever stand with equity till the first to breach it, a man of Banu Umayyah called Yazid.""** Makhul did not meet Abu Ubaydah."
"9237","Abdullah, meaning Ibn Masud, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that the Messenger passed a house with twelve men saying. > **""In this house is one whose trial upon my nation is worse than the trial of the Dajjal.""**"
"9238","Abdullah ibn Amr, may Allah be pleased with them both, reports that the Prophet said. > **""There shall be a caliph, he and his issue of Fire folk.""**"
"9239","Abdullah ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, reports that he went early to the Prophet, then Abul Hasan came and the Prophet said, draw near O Abul Hasan, drawing him till he whispered in his ear. Then the Prophet came to his left raising his head startled saying, the wicked knocked at the door with his hearing. He said, go O Abul Hasan leading him as a sheep led to its milker. Ali came with al-Hakam holding his ear and jaws together till he stood before the Prophet, and Allah's Prophet cursed him thrice. The Prophet said to Ali, seat him aside, till Muhajirun and Ansar came to the Prophet. Then he called him saying, this shall oppose Allah's Book and His Prophet's practice, and from his loins emerges one whose trial's smoke reaches heaven. A Muslim said, Allah and His Messenger spoke truth, is he too little and low for that. He said, yes, and some of you that day his partisans. > **""Go O Abul Hasan leading him as a sheep led to its milker. This shall oppose Allah's Book and His Prophet's practice, and from his loins emerges one whose trial's smoke reaches heaven.""**"
"9240","Nasr ibn Asim al-Laythi reports from his father that he entered Madinah mosque with people saying, we seek refuge in Allah from Allah's anger and His Messenger's. He asked what. They said, the Messenger preached on his minbar when a man rose taking his son's hand out of the mosque, and the Messenger said, may Allah curse the leader and the led. Woe to this nation one day from so-and-so of broad buttocks. > **""May Allah curse the leader and the led. Woe to this nation one day from so-and-so of broad buttocks.""**"
"9241","Amr ibn Murrah al-Juhani, a Companion, reports that al-Hakam ibn Abi al-As sought permission upon the Messenger, who knew his speech saying, permit him, upon him is curse of Allah, angels and all people. What emerges from his loins but their righteous, few, honoured in this world abased in Hereafter, folk of plotting and deceit. In another, what emerges from his loins but their righteous, few. Abu al-Hasan al-Jazari veiled, rest trustworthy. > **""Permit him, upon him is curse of Allah, angels and all people. What emerges from his loins but their righteous, few, honoured in this world abased in Hereafter, folk of plotting and deceit.""**"
"9242","Abdullah ibn Mawhab reports that he was with Muawiyah ibn Abi Sufyan when Marwan entered asking his needs, saying, fulfill my need O Amir al-Muminin, by Allah my burden is great, father of ten, brother of ten, uncle of ten. When Marwan turned, with Ibn Abbas sitting with Muawiyah on his couch, Muawiyah adjured, O Ibn Abbas, know you the Messenger said, when Bani Abi al-Hakam reach thirty men they take Allah's signs as fortune among them, Allah's servants as servants, His Book as intrusion. When they reach four hundred ninety-seven their ruin is swifter than a date. He said, O Allah yes. Marwan mentioned a need, then returned Abd al-Malik to Muawiyah speaking therein. When he turned Muawiyah adjured, O Ibn Abbas, know you the Messenger mentioned this saying, father of the four tyrants. He said, O Allah yes. Therefore Muawiyah claimed Ziyad. > **""When Bani Abi al-Hakam reach thirty men they take Allah's signs as fortune among them, Allah's servants as servants, His Book as intrusion. When they reach four hundred ninety-seven their ruin is swifter than a date. He is father of the four tyrants.""**"
"9243","Abdullah ibn Amr, may Allah be pleased with them both, reports that the Messenger said, the first to emerge upon you from this door is a man of Fire folk, and so-and-so emerged. In a version, a man shall surely emerge upon you raised on Resurrection upon other than my practice or my creed. He left his father home fearing it he, but another emerged and the Messenger said, it is this. > **""The first to emerge upon you from this door is a man of Fire folk. A man shall surely emerge upon you raised on the Day of Resurrection upon other than my practice.""**"
"9244","Abdur Rahman ibn Abi Bakr, may Allah be pleased with them both, reports that al-Hakam ibn Abi al-As sat with the Prophet, and when the Prophet spoke he twitched. The Prophet saw him saying, so you are, and he twitched till he died. > **""So you are.""**"
"9245","Hudhayfah, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that when the Prophet was taken and Abu Bakr made successor, he was spoken to of al-Hakam ibn Abi al-As, and he said, I would not untie a knot the Messenger tied."
"9246","Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that the Messenger saw in sleep as if Bani al-Hakam leaped upon his minbar descending, and mornings angered saying, why did I see Bani al-Hakam leaping upon my minbar like monkeys. After that the Messenger was never seen laughing fully till he died. > **""Why did I see Bani al-Hakam leaping upon my minbar like monkeys.""**"
"9247","Thawban, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that the Messenger said. > **""I was shown Bani Marwan alternating upon my minbar displeasing me, and Bani al-Abbas alternating upon my minbar pleasing me.""**"
"9248","Umm Hakim bint Amr ibn Sinan al-Jadaliyyah reports that al-Ashath ibn Qays sought permission upon Ali, and Qunbar repelled him bloodying his nose. Ali emerged asking, what is yours and his O Ashath. By Allah had you grappled a slave of Thaqif the hairs of your privates would bristle. Asked, O Amir al-Muminin, who is Thaqif's slave. He said, a boy ruling them leaving no Arab house but entering humiliation. Asked, how long he rules. He said, twenty if he reaches."
"9249","Thawban, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that the Messenger said. > **""Bani al-Abbas have two banners, its top disbelief and its centre error. If you reach it do not stray.""**"
"9250","Thawban, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that the Messenger said. > **""What are mine and Bani al-Abbas. They divide my nation, shed their blood and dress them black clothes. Allah dresses them clothes of Fire.""**"
"9251","Abu Umamah al-Bahili, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that the Messenger said, two banners shall emerge from the east for Bani al-Abbas, its first destroyed its last cut. Aid them not, may Allah aid them not. Whoever walks under their banner Allah admits him Hell on Resurrection. They are worst of Allah's creation and their followers worst. They claim they are of me, but I am free of them and they free of me. Their marks are long hair and black clothes. Sit them not in assembly, trade them not in markets, guide them not the road, water them not. Heaven folk are harmed by their takbir. > **""Two banners shall emerge from the east for Bani al-Abbas, its first destroyed its last cut. Aid them not, may Allah aid them not. Whoever walks under their banner Allah admits him Hell on the Day of Resurrection. They claim they are of me, but I am free of them and they free of me.""**"
"9252","Dawud ibn Abi Salih reports that Marwan came finding a man laying his face on the grave asking, know you what you do. He turned, it was Abu Ayyub, saying, yes I came to the Messenger not the stone. I heard the Messenger say. > **""Weep not over religion when its folk rule it. Weep over religion when other than its folk rule it.""**"
"9253","Zadhan Abu Umar reports from Ulaym that they sat on a roof with a Companion, Ulaym thought Abbas al-Ghifari, while people left in plague, and Abbas said thrice, O plague take me. Ulaym asked why, did the Messenger not say none wishes death at severance of his deed nor returned to seek amends. He said, I heard the Messenger say, hasten with death six: rule of fools, sale of judgment, belittling blood, severing kin, youth taking Quran as flutes advancing a man singing them though least in understanding. Ahmad, al-Bazzar, al-Tabarani in al-Awsat and al-Kabir similar, except from Abbas al-Ghifari, I heard the Messenger fearing upon his nation six traits: rule of boys, many police, bribery in judgment, severing kin, belittling blood, youth taking Quran as flutes advancing one not most understanding nor virtuous singing. > **""None of you wishes death at severance of his deed. Hasten with death six: rule of fools, sale of judgment, belittling blood, severing kin, youth taking Quran as flutes advancing a man singing them though least in understanding.""**"
"9254","Awf ibn Malik, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that the Prophet said. > **""I fear upon you six: rule of fools, shedding blood, sale of judgment, severing kin, youth taking Quran as flutes, and many police.""**"
"9255","Ilba al-Sulami, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that he heard the Messenger say. > **""The Hour shall not rise till a man of freedmen called Jahjah rules people.""**"
"9256","Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that the Messenger said. > **""Whoever dwells the desert is harsh, whoever follows hunting is heedless, whoever comes to sultans' gates is trialed. No servant nears the sultan but distances from Allah.""**"
"9257","Abdullah ibn al-Harith ibn Jaz al-Zubaydi, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that the Messenger said. > **""After me shall be a sultan of trials, upon whose doors as camel resting places. They give none anything but the like taken of his religion.""**"
"9258","A man of Bani Salma reports that the Messenger said. > **""Beware gates of sultans, for it has become hardship.""**"
"9259","Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, reports that the Messenger said. > **""Whoever attends a ruler, let him speak good or be silent.""**"
"9260","Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that the Messenger said. > **""O Abu Hurayrah, enter not upon rulers. If you are overcome thereby, exceed not my practice. Fear not their sword and whip to command them to fear Allah.""** The chapter preceded with other narrations."
"9261","Abu Said, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that the Prophet said, rulers with entourages and retinues lying and wronging. Whoever enters upon them affirming their lie aiding their wrong is not of me nor I of him. Whoever enters them not, affirms not their lie, aids not their wrong, is of me and I of him. Ahmad and Abu Yala add, I am free of him and he free of me. > **""Rulers with entourages and retinues lying and wronging. Whoever enters upon them affirming their lie aiding their wrong is not of me nor I of him. Whoever enters them not and aids them not is of me and I of him.""**"
"9262","Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, reports that the Messenger said, rulers after me over you commanding you what they practise not. Whoever affirms their lie aiding their wrong is not of me nor I of him, and shall never come to me at the Hawd. Ahmad and al-Bazzar say, the Prophet emerged with nine in the mosque, four freedmen five Arabs, saying, rulers over you, whoever aids their wrong affirming their lie frequenting their gates is not of me nor I of him, and shall never come to me at the Hawd. Whoever aids them not nor affirms is of me and I of him, and shall come to me at the Hawd. > **""Rulers after me over you commanding you what they practise not. Whoever affirms their lie aiding their wrong is not of me nor I of him, and shall never come to me at the Hawd.""**"
"9263","Jabir ibn Abdillah, may Allah be pleased with them both, reports that the Prophet said to Kab ibn Ujrah, may Allah protect you from rule of fools. He asked what is rule of fools. He said, rulers after me guided not by my guidance nor practising my practice. Whoever affirms their lie aiding their wrong, those are not of me nor I of them, nor coming to my Hawd. Whoever affirms them not nor aids is of me and I of them, and shall come to my Hawd. O Kab ibn Ujrah, fasting is a shield, charity extinguishes sin, prayer is nearness, or proof. O Kab ibn Ujrah, people are two mornings: self-buyer freeing it, or self-seller ruining it. Ahmad and al-Bazzar add, no flesh grown of unlawful enters Paradise, Fire worthier of it. > **""May Allah protect you from rule of fools. Rulers after me guided not by my guidance nor practising my practice. Whoever affirms their lie aiding their wrong is not of me nor I of them, nor coming to my Hawd. Whoever affirms them not is of me and I of them. Fasting is a shield, charity extinguishes sin, prayer is nearness. No flesh grown of unlawful enters Paradise, Fire is worthier of it.""**"
"9264","Al-Numan ibn Bashir, may Allah be pleased with them both, reports that the Messenger came out to them in the mosque after Isha raising his sight to heaven then lowering till they thought something happened in heaven, saying, rulers after me wronging and lying. Whoever affirms their lie aiding their wrong is not of me nor I of them. Whoever affirms them not nor aids is of me and I of him. Muslim blood is expiation. Glory be to Allah, praise be to Allah, no god but Allah, Allah is Greatest are the enduring good. He has another on enduring good in Ibn Majah. > **""Rulers after me wronging and lying. Whoever affirms their lie aiding their wrong is not of me nor I of them. Whoever affirms them not is of me and I of him. Muslim blood is expiation. Glory be to Allah, praise be to Allah, no god but Allah, Allah is Greatest are the enduring good.""**"
"9265","Hudhayfah, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that the Prophet said. > **""Rulers over you wronging and lying. Whoever affirms their lie aiding their wrong is not of me nor I of him, nor coming to me at the Hawd. Whoever affirms them not nor aids them is of me and I of him, and shall come to me at the Hawd.""**"
"9266","Khabbab, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that they sat at the Prophet's door and he emerged saying, do you hear. They said, we heard, twice or thrice. He said, rulers over you, affirm them not in their lie nor aid them in their wrong. Whoever affirms their lie aiding their wrong shall not come to me at the Hawd. > **""Do you hear. Rulers over you, affirm them not in their lie nor aid them in their wrong. Whoever affirms their lie aiding their wrong shall not come to me at the Hawd.""**"
"9267","Imran ibn Husayn, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that a bedouin told him he heard the Messenger say, I fear for Quraysh only themselves. He asked what is theirs. He said, miserly big-bellied. If your life prolongs you shall see them trialing people till people among them as sheep between two troughs, to this once and to this once. Long path in Khasais. > **""I fear for Quraysh only themselves. Miserly big-bellied. If your life prolongs you shall see them trialing people till people among them as sheep between two troughs, to this once and to this once.""**"
"9268","Imran ibn Husayn, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that the Messenger said, I fear for Quraysh only themselves. He asked what. He said, miserly big-bellied. If your life prolongs you see them trialing people till people among them as sheep between two troughs, once to this and once to this. > **""I fear for Quraysh only themselves. Miserly big-bellied. If your life prolongs you see them trialing people till people among them as sheep between two troughs.""**"
"9269","Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that the Messenger said. > **""Three Allah hates: a lying king, an arrogant destitute and a stingy rich.""**"
"9270","Abu Umamah, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that the Prophet said. > **""Revile not rulers and supplicate Allah for their rectitude, for their rectitude is your rectitude.""**"
"9271","Abu Musbih reports that he sat with Companions among them Shaddad ibn Aws and Thawban, freedman of the Messenger, recalling that the Messenger said, a man may do such good yet a hypocrite. They asked, O Messenger, how a hypocrite believing in you. He said, cursing rulers and reviling them. > **""A man may do such good yet a hypocrite. Cursing rulers and reviling them.""**"
"9272","Abu al-Darda, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that the Messenger said, Allah says, I am Allah, no god but I, Owner of kings and King of kings. Hearts of kings in My Hand. When servants obey Me I turn their kings' hearts upon them with kindness and mercy. When servants disobey Me I turn their hearts upon them with anger and vengeance, making them taste evil torment. Busy not yourselves supplicating against kings, but busy yourselves with remembrance and supplication, I suffice you your kings. > **""I am Allah, no god but I, Owner of kings and King of kings. Hearts of kings in My Hand. When servants obey Me I turn their kings' hearts upon them with kindness and mercy. When servants disobey Me I turn their hearts upon them with anger. Busy not yourselves supplicating against kings, but busy yourselves with remembrance and supplication, I suffice you your kings.""**"
"9273","Abu Humayd al-Saidi, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that the Messenger said. > **""Gifts to officials are ghulul.""** Preceding narrations on bribes passed in Judgments."
"9274","Abdullah, may Allah be pleased with him, said, when you are three on travel appoint one of you over you."
